CET.data.listeningByYear[2021] = [{"id":"L3","level":"CET4","type":"长对话","source":"2021年6月 · 四级 · 长对话","year":2021,"session":"6月","title":"周末志愿者招募","intro":"两人讨论社区图书馆周末阅读志愿项目的培训与任务安排。","audio":"assets/audio/2021/cet4-2021-06-set1.mp3","lines":[{"sp":"Q1","en":"And finally in tonight's news, a 9-year-old boy named Joe, told not to draw in class, wins a job decorating a restaurant with his drawings.","cn":"最后是今晚的新闻，一名9岁男孩Joe在课堂上被禁止画画，却凭借自己的画作赢得了一份装饰餐厅的工作。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Rather than shutting down the habit of drawing in his school's workbook, Joe's parents decided to encourage his creativity by sending their son to an after-school art class.","cn":"Joe的父母没有制止他在学校作业本上画画的习惯，而是决定鼓励他的创造力，送他去参加课后艺术班。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"His teacher recognized Joe's talent and posted all his work online, which led to something pretty wonderful.","cn":"他的老师认可了Joe的天赋，并把他所有的作品发布到网上，这带来了一件非常美好的事情。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"A restaurant named \"Number 4\" in Newcastle contacted Joe's teacher to ask if the 9-year-old could come and decorate its dining-room with his drawings.","cn":"Newcastle一家名为\"Number 4\"的餐厅联系了Joe的老师，询问这个9岁的孩子能否来用他的画作装饰餐厅的用餐区。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Every day after school, Joe's dad drives him to the restaurant so he can put his ideas straight on the wall.","cn":"每天放学后，Joe的爸爸开车送他去餐厅，这样他就可以把自己的创意直接画在墙上。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Once he's all done, the work will remain there permanently.","cn":"一旦全部完成，这些作品将永久保留在那里。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Joe's dad said Joe is a really talented little boy.","cn":"Joe的爸爸说Joe是一个非常有天赋的小男孩。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"He's excellent at school.","cn":"他在学校表现出色。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"He's great at football.","cn":"他足球踢得很好。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"But drawing is definitely what he is most passionate about.","cn":"但画画绝对是他最热爱的事情。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"Kirsteen Marshall, a 34-year-old mum of one, posted a tearful video on social media Wednesday, begging for the safe return of her beloved pet dog.","cn":"岁的单亲妈妈Kirsteen Marshall周三在社交媒体上发布了一段含泪视频,恳求安全归还她心爱的宠物狗。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"After combing through the security video outside a Gorbals shop, Kirsteen has now posted an image of a man suspected of stealing the dog.","cn":"在仔细查看Gorbals一家商店外的监控视频后,Kirsteen现已发布了一名涉嫌偷狗男子的照片。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"The image appears to show a man carrying the dog in his arms.","cn":"照片似乎显示一名男子抱着这只狗。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"Kirsteen also believes the video obtained from the shop shows the dog being stolen by a man before driving off in a car which had been waiting nearby.","cn":"Kirsteen还认为从商店获得的视频显示,这只狗被一名男子偷走,随后乘坐一辆在附近等候的汽车离开。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"The family is now offering a £5,000 reward for the safe return of the dog after launching a social media campaign to find the thief.","cn":"在发起社交媒体活动寻找窃贼后,这家人现在悬赏5000英镑以安全找回这只狗。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"The dog is six and a half years old and was last seen wearing a red collar.","cn":"这只狗六岁半,最后被看到时戴着红色项圈。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"Kirsteen said: \"We'll pay that to anyone who brings him home as long as they are not responsible for his disappearance.\"","cn":"Kirsteen说:\"只要他们不是对狗的失踪负有责任,我们会付钱给任何把它带回家的人。"},{"sp":"Q3","en":"Police are investigating the incident.","cn":"警方正在调查此事。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"London's Eggs & Bread café offers boiled eggs, toast, jam, and bacon, as well as tea, coffee and orange juice.","cn":"伦敦的Eggs & Bread咖啡馆提供煮鸡蛋、吐司、果酱和培根,以及茶、咖啡和橙汁。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"But at the end of the meal, customers don't have to worry about the bill.","cn":"但在用餐结束时,顾客不必担心账单。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Hungry customers can pay whatever amount they can afford to eat at the café, or nothing at all.","cn":"饥饿的顾客可以支付他们能承受的任何金额在这家咖啡馆用餐,或者什么都不付。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Owner Guy Wilson says his café aims to build community, rather than profits.","cn":"店主Guy Wilson说,他的咖啡馆旨在建立社区,而非追求利润。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"He wants to provide a bridge for people to connect in an area that has been divided by class and wealth by providing affordable breakfasts.","cn":"他希望通过提供人们负担得起的早餐,为这个被阶级和财富分割的地区的人们搭建一座连接的桥梁。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"The café is open in the mornings every day of the year and has two members of staff or supervisors on shift every day.","cn":"这家咖啡馆全年每天早上营业,每天有两名员工或主管值班。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"The café doesn't use volunteers, but pays its staff to ensure consistency in its service.","cn":"咖啡馆不使用志愿者,而是支付员工工资以确保服务的一致性。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"It doesn't take donations and doesn't want to be seen as a charity.","cn":"它不接受捐赠,也不希望被视为慈善机构。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Mr. Wilson says, when people start to know other people around them, they realize they're not that different.","cn":"Wilson先生说,当人们开始了解周围的其他人时,他们会意识到彼此并没有那么不同。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"And whatever their financial background, or their educational background, most people will have something in common with each other.","cn":"无论他们的经济背景或教育背景如何,大多数人都会与彼此有一些共同点。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"He says it's important that his café can offer his customers security and permanence.","cn":"他说,他的咖啡馆能够为顾客提供安全感和稳定性是很重要的。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"M: So what time do you think we should have the party on Saturday?","cn":"M: 那你觉得我们星期六的聚会应该定在什么时候？"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"W: How about inviting people to come at 6:00 p.m.?","cn":"W: 邀请大家下午6点来怎么样？"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"Then we'll have the afternoon to prepare food and drink, and stuff like that.","cn":"这样我们下午就有时间准备食物、饮料这些东西了。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"M: Yes, I was thinking that around 6:00 would be good too.","cn":"M: 是的,我也在想6点左右比较好。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"What food should we provide?","cn":"我们应该准备什么食物？"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"W: Well, I had thought about baking a cake, and some biscuits.","cn":"W: 嗯,我本来想烤个蛋糕,还有一些饼干。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"And now I think we should prepare some sandwiches and snacks, and some other kinds of food, so that people can just help themselves, rather than getting everyone to sit down at the table to eat a meal.","cn":"现在我觉得我们应该准备一些三明治和零食,还有其他种类的食物,这样大家可以自己取用,而不是让所有人都坐在餐桌前吃正餐。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"I think that's a bit too formal.","cn":"我觉得那样有点太正式了。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"It's better to let people walk around and talk to each other, or sit where they like.","cn":"最好让大家随意走动聊天,或者坐在他们喜欢的地方。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"M: Yes, that sounds good.","cn":"M: 好的,听起来不错。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"I'll go to the supermarket to get some drinks.","cn":"我去超市买些饮料。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"I think I might try that big new supermarket on the other side of town and see what they have.","cn":"我想去镇子另一边那家新开的大超市看看他们有什么。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"I've not been there before.","cn":"我以前没去过那儿。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"I think we should get some beer and wine, and some fruit juice, and other soft drinks.","cn":"我觉得我们应该买些啤酒和葡萄酒,还有一些果汁和其他软饮料。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"What do you think?","cn":"你觉得呢？"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"W: Sounds great.","cn":"W: 听起来很好。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"I think those drinks will be enough.","cn":"我觉得这些饮料就够了。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"And I heard that the new supermarket offers some big discounts to attract customers.","cn":"而且我听说那家新超市为了吸引顾客有很大的折扣。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"So going there should be a great idea.","cn":"所以去那里应该是个好主意。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"What should we do about music?","cn":"音乐方面我们怎么办？"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"M: Maybe we should ask Paul to bring his computer and speakers, so that we can play some music.","cn":"M: 也许我们应该让Paul带上他的电脑和音箱,这样我们就能放些音乐了。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"He has a great collection of different stuff.","cn":"他收藏了很多不同类型的音乐。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"W: Yes.","cn":"W: 好的。"},{"sp":"Q8","en":"All right.","cn":"行。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: I'm thinking of buying a car.","cn":"W: 我在考虑买辆车。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"I wouldn't need to use it every day, but I think it would be very convenient to have one for the weekends.","cn":"我不需要每天都用，但我觉得周末有辆车会很方便。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: That's exciting.","cn":"M: 那挺让人兴奋的。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Would this be your first car?","cn":"这会是你的第一辆车吗？"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: No, I actually owned a car for a little while when I lived in Miami.","cn":"W: 不是，实际上我在Miami住的时候拥有过一辆车，时间不长。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"You see in America, many cities don't have good public transport.","cn":"你知道在美国，很多城市的公共交通都不太好。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"So, most people need their own car to get around.","cn":"所以大多数人需要自己的车来出行。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: I see.","cn":"M: 我明白了。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"So have you got your mind set on a specific model?","cn":"那你心里有想好要哪个具体型号吗？"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: No, not really.","cn":"W: 没有，还没定。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"I've heard that German cars are very reliable, but I haven't decided on a specific model yet.","cn":"我听说德国车很可靠，但我还没决定具体型号。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"I'd also like it to be small, so that it's easy to drive in the city.","cn":"我还想要辆小点的，这样在城里开起来方便。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: I have a friend who sells second-hand cars.","cn":"M: 我有个朋友卖二手车。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"In fact, I think his family owns the business.","cn":"实际上，我觉得他家就是做这个生意的。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"He's a really nice guy, and he knows a lot about cars.","cn":"他人特别好，而且很懂车。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"I could give you his phone number if you want, and you could call him and ask him questions.","cn":"如果你愿意的话，我可以把他的电话号码给你，你可以打给他问问题。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: Hmm, that's nice of you, but I don't want to feel obliged to buy one of his cars.","cn":"W: 嗯，你人挺好的，但我不想觉得有义务必须买他的车。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: Oh, no, he's not like that.","cn":"M: 哦，不会的，他不是那样的人。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"He's a good friend of mine, and he would never try to pressure you or cheat you.","cn":"他是我的好朋友，他绝不会试图向你施压或者骗你。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"W: Well, if you trust him, then, I guess it should be OK.","cn":"W: 嗯，如果你信任他的话，那我想应该没问题。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"To be honest, I could use some help in deciding what type of vehicle would best suit my needs.","cn":"说实话，在决定什么类型的车最适合我的需求这方面，我确实需要一些帮助。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Speaking to an expert would be a good idea.","cn":"跟专家聊聊会是个好主意。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"M: Exactly.","cn":"M: 没错。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"You have nothing to worry about.","cn":"你完全不用担心。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"He's a lovely guy, and he'll be happy to help.","cn":"他人很好，会很乐意帮忙的。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Pigs are not native to North America.","cn":"猪并非北美洲的原生物种。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They were first introduced to California by Spanish and Russian explorers and settlers many centuries ago.","cn":"它们最早是在许多世纪前由西班牙和俄罗斯的探险者及定居者引入加利福尼亚的。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"In the early times, pigs were allowed to wander freely in search of food.","cn":"在早期,猪被允许自由游荡觅食。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"This practice also allowed many pigs to escape from farms and live in the wild, which became a problem.","cn":"这种做法也使许多猪从农场逃脱并在野外生活,这成为了一个问题。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"In fact, as one of the most damaging invasive species on the continent, wild pigs cause millions of dollars in crop damage yearly.","cn":"事实上,作为该大陆上破坏性最强的入侵物种之一,野猪每年造成数百万美元的作物损失。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They also harbor dozens of diseases that threaten both humans and farm animals.","cn":"它们还携带数十种威胁人类和家畜的疾病。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Forest patches with wild pigs have been found to have considerably reduced plant and animal diversity.","cn":"有野猪出没的林地被发现植物和动物多样性大幅减少。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"In addition to either eating other animals or their food supply, wild pigs damage native habitats by rooting up grasses and rubbing on trees.","cn":"除了吃掉其他动物或它们的食物来源外,野猪还通过拱掘草地和摩擦树木破坏原生栖息地。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Their activities may also create opportunities for invasive plants to colonize these areas.","cn":"它们的活动也可能为入侵植物在这些地区定殖创造机会。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Wild pigs will eat almost anything containing calories.","cn":"野猪几乎会吃任何含有热量的东西。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Mice, deer, birds, snakes and frogs are among their victims.","cn":"老鼠、鹿、鸟类、蛇和青蛙都是它们的受害者。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They can also harm other wild species through indirect competition, rather than eating them or shrinking their food supply.","cn":"它们还可以通过间接竞争而非吃掉其他野生物种或减少其食物供应来伤害它们。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"On one particular United States island, wild pigs themselves became an attractive food source for a species of mainland eagle.","cn":"在美国的一个特定岛屿上,野猪本身成为了一种大陆鹰的诱人食物来源。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The eagles began breeding on the island, and also feeding on a species of native fox.","cn":"这些鹰开始在岛上繁殖,并且也以一种本地狐狸为食。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The foxes were almost wiped out completely.","cn":"这些狐狸几乎被完全消灭。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"A pair of entrepreneurs are planning to build and launch a spacecraft that would carry and roast coffee beans in outer space.","cn":"一对创业者正计划建造并发射一艘航天器，用于在外太空中携带并烘焙咖啡豆。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The craft will use the heat of re-entry to roast coffee beans as they float inside it in a pressurised tank.","cn":"该航天器将利用再入大气层时产生的热量来烘焙咖啡豆,豆子会在一个加压舱内漂浮。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The effect would be to roast the beans all over, and produce perfect coffee.","cn":"这种方式能够全方位烘焙咖啡豆,制作出完美的咖啡。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The businessmen say that on Earth, beans can easily break apart and get burned in the roaster.","cn":"这两位商人表示,在地球上,咖啡豆在烘焙机中很容易破碎和烧焦。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"But if gravity is removed, the beans float around in a heated oven, receiving 360 degrees of evenly distributed heat and roast to near perfection.","cn":"但如果去除重力,咖啡豆就会在加热的烤箱中四处漂浮,接受360度均匀分布的热量,烘焙至近乎完美的状态。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The spacecraft will reach a height of around 200 km.","cn":"航天器将到达约200公里的高度。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The beans would then be roasted in the heat generated by the craft's 20-minute re-entry into Earth's atmosphere.","cn":"随后咖啡豆将在航天器重返地球大气层的20分钟过程中,利用产生的热量进行烘焙。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Temperatures in the pressurised tank will be kept to around 200℃.","cn":"加压舱内的温度将保持在200℃左右。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Once back on Earth, the planet's first space-roasted beans would be used to make coffee that would be sold for the first time in Dubai.","cn":"返回地球后,这些地球上首批太空烘焙的咖啡豆将被用来制作咖啡,并首次在Dubai销售。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"This is where the pair's company is based.","cn":"这正是这对创业者公司的所在地。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"It is not clear how much they would charge for a cup.","cn":"目前尚不清楚他们会对一杯咖啡收取多少费用。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Surprisingly, the Space Roaster concept—should it go ahead—will not be the first attempt to take coffee into space.","cn":"令人惊讶的是,Space Roaster概念——如果能够实施的话——将不是首次尝试将咖啡带入太空。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"In 2015, two Italian companies collaborated on the construction of a similar type of spacecraft, which was the first coffee machine designed for use in space.","cn":"2015年,两家意大利公司合作建造了一种类似的航天器,那是首台为太空使用而设计的咖啡机。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"In cold and snowy Alaska, there's a village called Takotna.","cn":"在寒冷多雪的阿拉斯加，有一个名叫Takotna的村庄。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"It has a population of a mere 49 souls.","cn":"它的人口仅有49人。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Each March, this tiny village swells up in numbers, because it is located in the middle of a race that takes place every year.","cn":"每年三月，这个小村庄的人数会激增，因为它位于一年一度举行的比赛路线中途。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"It is a seven-day race, called the Iditarod Trail, and participants stop at Takotna for their obligatory 24-hour rest.","cn":"这是一场为期七天的比赛，名为Iditarod Trail，参赛者会在Takotna停留进行规定的24小时休息。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Lucky for them, Takotna is famous for its delicious fruit pies.","cn":"对他们来说幸运的是，Takotna以其美味的水果派而闻名。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Weeks before the competitors arrive, the residents of Takotna start preparing for what is without question their biggest event of the year.","cn":"在参赛者到来前几周，Takotna的居民就开始为这场毫无疑问是他们全年最盛大的活动做准备。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The whole village chips in to help, including the kids, who end up developing their baking skills at an early age.","cn":"全村人都参与帮忙，包括孩子们，他们因此在很小的时候就开始培养烘焙技能。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The exhausted and hungry racers are greeted with delightful pies of all kinds, such as apple, orange, lemon or banana.","cn":"筋疲力尽且饥肠辘辘的参赛者会受到各种美味派的款待，比如苹果派、橙子派、柠檬派或香蕉派。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"They consume the pies as stomach warming race fuel.","cn":"他们将这些派作为暖胃的比赛燃料来食用。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The toughness of the race allows for racers to eat pretty much whatever they want.","cn":"比赛的艰苦程度使得参赛者几乎可以想吃什么就吃什么。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The more calories, the better.","cn":"卡路里越高越好。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Takotna has gained a reputation for its dessert-based hospitality since the 1970s.","cn":"自20世纪70年代以来，Takotna因其以甜点为特色的热情好客而声名远扬。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"It started with one person, Jan Newton.","cn":"这一切始于一个人，Jan Newton。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Jan moved from Idaho with her husband in 1972 and opened a restaurant.","cn":"Jan和她的丈夫在1972年从Idaho搬来，并开了一家餐厅。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Her rich and filling-fruit pies quickly got the racers' attention, and the village gained some fame as a result.","cn":"她制作的香浓饱腹的水果派很快引起了参赛者的注意，村庄也因此获得了一些名气。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Proud residents then started to refer to Jan as Queen of Takotna.","cn":"自豪的居民随后开始称Jan为Takotna女王。"}],"questions":[{"q":"What is the woman interested in?","options":["A weekend reading program","A cooking class","A paid job at a library","A drawing competition"],"answer":0,"explain":"女士一开始就问社区图书馆周末阅读活动是否还在招志愿者，说明她感兴趣的是这个阅读项目。"},{"q":"What does the man say is required of volunteers?","options":["A teaching certificate","Patience and a clear voice","One year of experience","A university degree"],"answer":1,"explain":"男士说 they only ask for patience and a clear voice，只要求耐心和清楚的声音，不需要经验。"},{"q":"How long is the commitment?","options":["Four weekends this term","Two evenings a week","The whole year","One weekend per month"],"answer":0,"explain":"原文说 Just four weekends this term，本学期只需四个周末。"}],"cloze":[{"text":"Are they still looking for ______?","answers":["volunteers"],"hint":"志愿者"},{"text":"The training ______ is on Wednesday evening.","answers":["session"],"hint":"培训场次"},{"text":"They will ______ you with an experienced volunteer.","answers":["pair"],"hint":"把……配对"}]},{"id":"L8","level":"CET6","type":"短文","source":"2021年6月 · 六级 · 短文","year":2021,"session":"6月","title":"海洋塑料的来源","intro":"短文说明海洋塑料污染的来源、微塑料的危害与治理思路。","audio":"assets/audio/2021/cet6-2021-06-set1.mp3","lines":[{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: It's my last day at work tomorrow.","cn":"M: 明天是我在这儿工作的最后一天。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"I'll start my new job in two weeks.","cn":"两周后我就要开始新工作了。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"My human resources manager wants to conduct an interview with me before I leave.","cn":"人力资源经理想在我离职前和我进行一次面谈。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: Ah, an exit interview.","cn":"W: 啊，离职面谈。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Are you looking forward to it?","cn":"你期待吗？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: I'm not sure how I feel about it.","cn":"M: 我也说不清自己是什么感觉。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"I resigned because I've been unhappy at that company for a long time, but I'm not sure if I should tell them how I really feel.","cn":"我辞职是因为我在那家公司长期以来一直很不开心，但我不确定自己是否应该告诉他们真实的感受。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: To my way of thinking, there are two main potential benefits that come from unleashing an agitated stream of truth during an exit interview.","cn":"W: 在我看来，在离职面谈时把一股激动的真实想法倾泻出来，可能有两个主要好处。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"The first is release.","cn":"第一个是释放。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Unburdening yourself of frustration, and perhaps even anger to someone who isn't a friend or close colleague can be wonderfully freeing.","cn":"把自己的挫败感，甚至愤怒，倾诉给一个既不是朋友也不是关系亲密的同事的人，可能会让你感到如释重负。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: And let me guess.","cn":"M: 让我猜猜。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"The second is that the criticism will, theoretically, help the organization I'm leaving to improve, making sure employees of the future are less likely to encounter what I did?","cn":"第二个好处是，这些批评理论上会帮助我即将离开的组织改进，从而确保未来的员工不太可能遇到我所经历的那些问题？"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: That's right.","cn":"W: 没错。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"But the problem with the company improvement part is that very often it doesn't happen.","cn":"但公司改进这一点的问题在于，很多时候它并不会发生。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"An exit interview is supposed to be private, but often isn't.","cn":"离职面谈本应是私下进行的，但往往并不是。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"In my company, the information gained from these interviews is often not confidential.","cn":"在我所在的公司，从这些面谈中获得的信息通常并不保密。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"And the information is used as dirt against another manager, or can be traded among senior managers.","cn":"这些信息会被用来攻击另一位经理，或者在高层经理之间互相交换。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: Now you've got me rethinking what I'll disclose in the interview.","cn":"M: 你现在让我重新考虑面谈时要透露些什么了。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"There is always a chance that it could affect my reputation and my ability to network in the industry.","cn":"我的名声和我在这个行业建立人脉的能力，总有可能受到影响。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"It is a pretty small industry after all.","cn":"毕竟这个行业相当小。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: Anything you initially gain from the instant satisfaction of telling it like it is, you might lose down the track by injuring your future career prospects.","cn":"W: 你最初因为直抒己见而获得的即时满足，可能会因为损害未来的职业发展前景而在以后失去。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"M: Right.","cn":"M: 对。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Perhaps it would be better getting things off my chest by going to one of those rate-your-employer websites.","cn":"也许去那些给雇主评分的网站发泄一下，会更好一些。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"W: You could.","cn":"W: 你可以这么做。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"And don't do the interview at all.","cn":"也可以完全不参加面谈。"},{"sp":"Q1","en":"Exit interviews are not mandatory.","cn":"离职面谈不是强制性的。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: Today, I'm talking to the renowned botanist, Jane Forster.","cn":"M: 今天，我要采访著名植物学家 Jane Forster。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: Thank you for inviting me to join you on the show, Henry.","cn":"W: Henry，谢谢你邀请我参加你的节目。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: Recently, Jane, you've become quite a celebrity since the release of your latest documentary.","cn":"M: 最近，Jane，自从你最新的纪录片上映以来，你已经成了相当有名的人。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Can you tell us a little about it?","cn":"能给我们介绍一下这部纪录片吗？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: Well, it follows my expedition to study the vegetation indigenous to the rainforest in equatorial areas of Southeast Asia.","cn":"W: 这部纪录片记录了我在东南亚赤道地区的热带雨林中，考察当地原生植被的一次探险。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: You certainly get to travel to some very exotic locations.","cn":"M: 你确实有机会去一些非常异国情调的地方旅行。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: It was far from glamorous, to be honest.","cn":"W: 老实说，那一点也不光鲜。我们去的地方只能乘独木舟到达，而且小屋里的生活条件至少可以说是很原始。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"The area we visited was accessible only by canoe and the living conditions in the hut were primitive, to say the least.","cn":"那里没有电，我们的水源就是附近的一条溪流。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"There was no electricity.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"And our water supply was a nearby stream.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: How were the weather conditions while you were there?","cn":"M: 你们在那里时的天气状况怎么样？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: The weather was not conducive to our work at all, since the humidity was almost unbearable.","cn":"W: 天气完全不利于我们的工作，因为空气湿度几乎让人无法忍受。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"At midday, we stayed in the hut and did nothing.","cn":"中午时分，我们就待在小屋里，什么也不做。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"It was too humid to either work or sleep.","cn":"天气太潮湿了，既没法工作，也没法睡觉。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: How long did your team spend in the jungle?","cn":"M: 你们团队在丛林里待了多久？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: Originally, we planned to be there for a month.","cn":"W: 我们原本计划在那里待一个月，但最后只待了两个星期。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"But in the end, we stayed for only two weeks.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: Why did you cut the expedition short?","cn":"M: 你们为什么提前结束了这次探险？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: Halfway through the trip, we received news that a hurricane was approaching.","cn":"W: 旅程过半时，我们收到消息说一场飓风正在逼近，所以不得不在极短的时间内撤离。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"And we had to evacuate at very short notice.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: That sounds like a fascinating anecdote.","cn":"M: 听起来真是个引人入胜的故事。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: It was frightening.","cn":"W: 当时很吓人。最快的撤离路线要经过湍急的河流，我们不得不带着所有设备穿过急流。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"The fastest evacuation route was through river rapids.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"We had to navigate them carrying all of our equipment.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: So overall, was the journey unsuccessful?","cn":"M: 那总的来说，这次旅程算是失败了吗？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: Absolutely not.","cn":"W: 当然不是。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"We gathered a massive amount of data about the local plant life.","cn":"我们收集了大量有关当地植物的资料。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: Why do you put up with such adverse conditions?","cn":"M: 你为什么能忍受如此恶劣的条件？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: Botany is an obsession for me.","cn":"W: 植物学对我来说是一种痴迷。我去过的许多地方都有令人惊叹的景色，而且我还能结识来自世界各地的各种各样的人。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Many of the destinations I visit have stunning scenery.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"And I get to meet a variety of people from all over the world.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: So where will your next destination be?","cn":"M: 那么，你的下一个目的地会是哪里？"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"W: I haven't decided yet.","cn":"W: 我还没决定。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"M: Then we can leave it for another occasion.","cn":"M: 那我们下次再聊。"},{"sp":"Q5","en":"Thanks.","cn":"谢谢。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Scientists often use specialized jargon terms while communicating with laymen.","cn":"科学家在与非专业人士交流时，常常使用专业术语。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Most of them don't realize the harmful effects of this practice.","cn":"他们中的大多数人没有意识到这种做法会产生有害影响。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"In a new study, people exposed to jargon when reading about subjects like autonomous vehicles and surgical robots later said they were less interested in science than others who read about the same topics, but without the use of specialized terms.","cn":"一项新的研究显示，在阅读有关自动驾驶汽车和手术机器人等主题的内容时接触到专业术语的人，后来表示自己对科学的兴趣低于阅读相同主题但未使用专业术语的人。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"They also felt less informed about science and less qualified to discuss science topics.","cn":"他们还觉得自己对科学的了解更少，也没有足够的资格讨论科学话题。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"It's noteworthy that it made no difference if the jargon terms were defined in the text.","cn":"值得注意的是，专业术语是否在文中得到定义并没有造成任何差异。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Even when the terms were defined, readers still felt the same lack of engagement as readers who read jargon that wasn't explained.","cn":"即使这些术语得到了解释，读者仍然感到自己与内容缺乏联系，就像那些阅读了未加解释的专业术语的读者一样。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"The problem is that the mere presence of jargon sends a discouraging message to readers.","cn":"问题在于，专业术语的存在本身就会向读者传递一种令人气馁的信息。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Hillary Schulman, the author of the study, asserts that specialized words are a signal.","cn":"该研究的作者希拉里·舒尔曼认为，专业词汇是一种信号。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Jargon tells people that the message isn't for them.","cn":"专业术语会告诉人们，这条信息不是为他们准备的。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"There's an even darker side to how people react to jargon.","cn":"人们对专业术语的反应还有更为严重的一面。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"In another study, researchers found that reading scientific articles containing jargon led people to doubt the actual science.","cn":"在另一项研究中，研究人员发现，阅读含有专业术语的科学文章会使人们怀疑科学本身。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"They found the opposite when a text is easier to read.","cn":"当文本更容易阅读时，他们发现的结果则恰恰相反。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Then people are more persuaded.","cn":"这样一来，人们会更容易被说服。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Thus, it's important to communicate clearly when talking about complex science subjects.","cn":"因此，在谈论复杂的科学主题时，清晰地进行交流非常重要。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"This is especially true with issues related to public health, like the safety of new medications and the benefits of vaccines.","cn":"涉及公共卫生的问题尤其如此，例如新药的安全性和疫苗的益处。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"Schulman concedes that the use of jargon is appropriate with scientific audiences.","cn":"舒尔曼承认，在面向科学界人士时使用专业术语是恰当的。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"But scientists who want to communicate with the general public need to modify their language.","cn":"但希望与公众交流的科学家需要调整自己的语言。"},{"sp":"Q9","en":"They need to eliminate jargon.","cn":"他们需要消除专业术语。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"At the beginning of the twentieth century, on the Gulf Coast in the US state of Texas, there was a hill where gas leakage was so noticeable that schoolboys would sometimes set the hill on fire.","cn":"二十世纪初，在美国得克萨斯州的墨西哥湾沿岸，有一座山丘，那里天然气泄漏十分明显，以至于学生们有时会把山丘点燃。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Pattillo Higgins, a disreputable local businessman, became convinced that there was oil below the gassy hill.","cn":"帕蒂洛·希金斯是一名声名狼藉的当地商人，他确信这座冒气的山丘下方有石油。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Oil wells weren't drilled back then; they were essentially dug.","cn":"那时还没有钻探油井；油井基本上是挖出来的。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"The sand under the hill defeated several attempts by Higgins' workers to make a proper hole.","cn":"山丘下的沙土使希金斯的工人几次试图挖出合适井孔的努力都以失败告终。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Higgins had forecast oil at 1,000 feet, a totally made-up figure.","cn":"希金斯预言一千英尺深处会有石油，这个数字完全是凭空捏造的。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Higgins subsequently hired a mining engineer, Captain Anthony Lucas.","cn":"随后，希金斯聘请了一名采矿工程师安东尼·卢卡斯上尉。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"After encountering several setbacks, Captain Lucas decided to use a drill, and his innovations created the modern oil drilling industry.","cn":"在经历了几次挫折后，卢卡斯上尉决定使用钻机，他的创新创造了现代石油钻探业。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"In January 1901, at 1,020 feet-almost precisely the depth predicted by Higgins' wild guess—the well roared and suddenly ejected mud and six tons of drilling pipe out of the ground, terrifying those present.","cn":"年1月，在一千零二十英尺深处——几乎正是希金斯那个荒唐猜测所预言的深度——油井发出轰鸣，突然将泥浆和六吨钻管从地下喷出，把在场的人吓坏了。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"For the next nine days, until the well was capped, the well poured out more oil than all the wells in America combined.","cn":"在接下来的九天里，直到油井被封住为止，它涌出的石油超过了美国所有油井产量的总和。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"In those days, Texas was almost entirely rural, with no large cities and practically no industry; cotton and beef were the foundation of the economy.","cn":"那时，得克萨斯州几乎完全是农村地区，没有大城市，实际上也没有工业；"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"Higgins' well changed that.","cn":"棉花和牛肉是经济的基础。希金斯的油井改变了这一切。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"The boom made some prospectors millionaires, but the sudden surplus of petroleum was not entirely a blessing for Texas.","cn":"这场繁荣使一些勘探者成为百万富翁，但石油突然过剩对得克萨斯州而言并不完全是福音。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"In the 1930s, prices crashed, to the point that in some parts of the country oil was cheaper than water.","cn":"到了20世纪30年代，油价暴跌，在美国一些地区，石油甚至比水还便宜。"},{"sp":"Q12","en":"That would become a familiar pattern of the boom-or-bust Texas' economy.","cn":"这后来成为得克萨斯州经济繁荣或萧条的一个常见模式。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Most people dislike their jobs.","cn":"大多数人不喜欢自己的工作。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"It's an astonishing but statistical fact.","cn":"这是一个令人惊讶却有统计数据支持的事实。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"A primary cause of employee dissatisfaction, according to fresh research, is that many believe they have terrible managers.","cn":"根据最新研究，员工不满的一个主要原因是，许多人认为自己的经理非常糟糕。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Few describe their managers as malicious or manipulative though.","cn":"不过，很少有人把自己的经理描述为恶意或善于操纵他人的人。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"While those types certainly exist, they are a minority.","cn":"虽然这类人确实存在，但他们只是少数。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The majority of managers, seemingly, just don't know any better.","cn":"显然，大多数经理只是缺乏更好的管理方法。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They are often emulating bad managers they've had in the past.","cn":"他们往往是在模仿自己过去遇到过的糟糕经理。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"It's likely they've never read a management book or attended a management course.","cn":"他们很可能从未读过管理类书籍，也没有参加过管理课程。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"They might not have even reflected on what good management looks like and how it would influence their own management style.","cn":"他们甚至可能从未认真思考过良好的管理应该是什么样，以及良好的管理会如何影响自己的管理风格。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The researchers interviewed employees about their managers, beginning with a question about the worst manager they had ever had.","cn":"研究人员就经理的表现采访了员工，首先询问他们曾经遇到过的最糟糕的经理。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"From this, the researchers came up with four main causes of why some managers are perceived as being simply awful at their jobs.","cn":"根据这些访谈，研究人员归纳出一些经理被认为工作能力极差的四个主要原因。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The first cause was company culture, which was seen by employees as enabling poor management practices.","cn":"第一个原因是企业文化，员工认为企业文化助长了糟糕的管理方式。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"It was specifically stressful work environments, minimal training and a lack of accountability that were found to be the most blameworthy.","cn":"研究发现，最应受指责的具体因素是压力很大的工作环境、极少的培训以及缺乏问责。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Often a manager's superiors can effectively encourage a manager's distasteful behavior when they fail to discipline the person's wrongdoings.","cn":"经理的上级在未能惩处经理的不当行为时，往往实际上是在助长这种令人反感的行为。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Such workplaces are sometimes described as toxic.","cn":"这类工作场所有时被称为有毒的工作环境。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The second cause was attributed to the managers' characteristics.","cn":"第二个原因归结于经理自身的特点。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"Those deemed to be most destructive were odd people—those without drive, those who allow personal problems into the workplace, and those with an unpleasant temperament or personality in general.","cn":"被认为最具破坏性的是一些古怪的人——缺乏进取心的人、把个人问题带入工作场所的人，以及总体上脾气或性格令人不快的人。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The third cause of poor management was associated with a deficiency of qualifications not so much the formal variety one obtains from a university, but the informal variety that comes from credible work experience and professional accomplishments.","cn":"管理不善的第三个原因与资历不足有关，这里的资历并不主要指从大学获得的正式学历，而是指通过可信的工作经历和职业成就积累起来的非正式资历。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The fourth cause concerned managers who've been promoted for reasons other than potential.","cn":"第四个原因涉及那些因潜力以外的理由而获得晋升的经理。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"One reason in particular why these people had been promoted was that they had been around the longest.","cn":"其中一个特别的原因是，他们在公司待的时间最长。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"It wasn't their skill set or other merits that got them the job; it was their tenure.","cn":"让他们得到这份工作的并不是他们的技能或其他优点，而是他们的任职年限。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"A point worth making is that the study was based only on the perspective of employees.","cn":"值得指出的是，这项研究仅基于员工的视角。研究人员没有询问高层领导如何看待他们的一线经理。"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"The researchers didn't ask senior leaders what they thought of their frontline managers.","cn":"他们很可能对自己提拔的人如今的表现感到满意，却完全没有意识到这些人实际上造成的损害；"},{"sp":"Q16","en":"It's quite possible they're content with how the individuals they promoted are now performing, merrily ignorant of the damage they're actually causing, which might explain why, as the researchers conclude, those same middle managers are usually unaware that they are a bad manager.","cn":"这或许可以解释为什么研究人员得出结论认为，那些同样的中层经理通常并不知道自己是一名糟糕的经理。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"With the use of driverless vehicles seemingly inevitable, mining companies in the vast Australian desert state of Western Australia are definitely taking the lead.","cn":"随着无人驾驶车辆的使用似乎已不可避免，位于澳大利亚广袤沙漠州西澳大利亚州的矿业公司无疑走在了前列。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Iron ore is a key ingredient in steel-making.","cn":"铁矿石是炼钢的关键原料。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The mining companies here produce almost 300 million tons of iron ore a year.","cn":"这里的矿业公司每年生产近3亿吨铁矿石。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The 240 giant autonomous trucks in use, in the Western Australian mines, can weigh 400 tons, fully loaded, and travel at speeds of up to 60 kilometers per hour.","cn":"西澳大利亚州矿区正在使用的240辆巨型自动驾驶卡车满载时重量可达400吨，行驶速度最高可达每小时60公里。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"They are a technological leap, transporting iron ore along routes which run for hundreds of kilometers from mines to their destinations.","cn":"它们是技术上的一大飞跃，沿着数百公里长的路线，将铁矿石从矿山运往目的地。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Here when the truck arrives at its destination, staff in the operation center direct it precisely where to unload.","cn":"当卡车抵达目的地时，运营中心的工作人员会精确指挥它在指定位置卸货。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Vast quantities of iron ore are then transported by autonomous trains to ocean ports.","cn":"随后，大量铁矿石由自动驾驶列车运往海港。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Advocates argue these automated vehicles will change mining forever.","cn":"支持者认为，这些自动化车辆将永远改变采矿业。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"It may only be five years before the use of automation technology leads to a fully robotic mine.","cn":"自动化技术的应用可能只需五年就会促成一座完全由机器人运作的矿山。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"A range of factors has pushed Western Australia's desert region to the lead of this automation revolution.","cn":"多种因素推动西澳大利亚的沙漠地区走在这场自动化革命的前沿。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"These include the huge size of the mines, the scale of equipment and the repetitive nature of some of the work.","cn":"这些因素包括矿山规模庞大、设备规模巨大，以及部分工作具有重复性。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Then there's the area's remoteness.","cn":"此外，还有该地区地处偏远这一因素。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"At 502,000 square kilometers, it can sometimes make recruiting staff a challenge.","cn":"这里面积达50.2万平方公里，有时会使招聘员工成为一项挑战。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Another consideration is the risks when humans interact with large machinery.","cn":"另一个需要考虑的因素是人类与大型机械互动时所面临的风险。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"There are also the financial imperatives.","cn":"此外还有财务方面的迫切需求。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The ongoing push by the mining corporations to be more productive and more efficient is another powerful driver in embracing automation technology.","cn":"矿业公司持续推动提高生产率和效率，也是其积极采用自动化技术的另一个强大动力。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The concept of a fully autonomous mine is a bit of a misleading term, however.","cn":"不过，将完全自动化的矿山称为“完全自主矿山”有些误导。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"This is because the more technology is put into the field, the more people are needed to deploy, maintain and improve it.","cn":"因为投入现场的技术越多，就越需要更多人员来部署、维护和改进这些技术。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The automation and digitization of the industry are creating a need for different jobs.","cn":"行业的自动化和数字化正在催生对不同岗位的需求，其中包括数据科学家以及从事自动化和人工智能工作的工程师。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"These include data scientists and engineers in automation and artificial intelligence.","cn":"矿业公司声称，自动化和机器人技术为实现更加可持续、更安全的采矿创造了机会。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"The mining companies claim automation and robotics present opportunities to make mining more sustainable and safer.","cn":"员工将获得一份更加充实、回报也更加丰厚的职业。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Employees will be offered a career that is even more fulfilling and more rewarding.","cn":""},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Workers' unions have accepted the inevitability of the introduction of new technology.","cn":"工人协会已经接受新技术引入的必然性。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"But they still have reservations about the rise of automation technology.","cn":"但它们仍然对自动化技术的发展持保留态度。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"Their main concern is the potential impact on remote communities.","cn":"它们最主要的担忧是自动化可能对偏远社区造成的影响。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"As automation spreads further, the question is how these remote communities will survive when the old jobs are eliminated.","cn":"随着自动化进一步普及，问题在于，当原有工作岗位被取消后，这些偏远社区将如何生存。"},{"sp":"Q19","en":"And this may well prove to be the most significant impact of robotic technology in many places around the world.","cn":"而这很可能会成为机器人技术在世界许多地方产生的最重大的影响。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"According to official statistics, Thailand's annual road-death rate is almost double the global average.","cn":"根据官方统计，泰国每年的道路死亡率几乎是全球平均水平的两倍。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Thai people know that their roads are dangerous, but they don't know this could easily be changed.","cn":"泰国人知道本国道路十分危险，但他们不知道这种状况其实很容易改变。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Globally, road accidents kill more people every year than any infectious disease.","cn":"在全球范围内，道路事故每年造成的死亡人数超过任何一种传染病。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Researchers at the Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation in America put the death toll in 2017 at 1.24 million.","cn":"美国健康指标与评估研究所的研究人员估计，2017年的死亡人数为124万。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"According to the institute, the overall number of deaths has been more or less static since the turn of the century.","cn":"据该研究所称，自本世纪初以来，死亡总人数基本保持不变。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"But that disguises a lot of changes in individual countries.","cn":"但这一数字掩盖了各个国家发生的诸多变化。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"In many poor countries, road accidents are killing more people than ever before.","cn":"在许多贫穷国家，道路事故造成的死亡人数比以往任何时候都多。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Those countries have swelling, young populations, a fast-growing fleet of cars and motorbikes, and a limited supply of surgeons.","cn":"这些国家人口不断增长且较为年轻，汽车和摩托车数量快速增加，而外科医生数量有限。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"It is impossible to know for sure because official statistics are so inadequate, but deaths are thought to have risen by 40% since 1990 in many low-income countries.","cn":"由于官方统计数据严重不足，无法确切得知实际情况，但据认为，许多低收入国家的死亡人数自1990年以来增加了40%。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"In many rich countries, by contrast, roads are becoming even safer.","cn":"相比之下，在许多富裕国家，道路正变得更加安全。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"In Estonia and Ireland, for example, the number of deaths has fallen by about two-thirds since the late 1990s.","cn":"例如，在爱沙尼亚和爱尔兰，死亡人数自20世纪90年代末以来减少了约三分之二。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"But the most important and intriguing changes are taking place in middle-income countries, which contain most of the world's people and have some of the most dangerous roads.","cn":"但最重要、也最引人关注的变化发生在中等收入国家。这些国家拥有世界上大多数人口，也有一些最危险的道路。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"According to researchers, in China and South Africa, traffic deaths have been falling since 2000, and in India since 2012, and the Philippines reached its peak four years ago.","cn":"据研究人员称，在中国和南非，交通事故死亡人数自2000年以来一直在下降；在印度，这一趋势始于2012年；"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The question is whether Thailand can soon follow suit.","cn":"菲律宾则在四年前达到峰值。问题在于，泰国能否很快步其后尘。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Rob MeInerney, head of the International Road Assessment Programme, says that all countries tend to go through three phases.","cn":"International Road Assessment Programme负责人Rob MeInerney表示，所有国家往往都会经历三个阶段。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"They begin with poor, slow roads.","cn":"第一阶段是道路状况差、通行速度慢。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"In the second phase, as they grow wealthier, they pave the roads, allowing traffic to move faster and pushing up the death rate.","cn":"第二阶段，随着国家变得更加富裕，道路得到铺设，车辆行驶速度加快，死亡率也随之上升。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Lastly, in the third phase, countries act to make their roads safer.","cn":"最后，在第三阶段，各国采取措施提高道路安全性。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The trick, then, is to reach the third stage sooner, by focusing earlier and more closely on fatal accidents.","cn":"因此，关键在于更早、更集中地关注致命事故，从而尽快进入第三阶段。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"How to do that?","cn":"如何做到这一点？"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"The solution lies not just in better infrastructure, but in better social incentives.","cn":"解决办法不仅在于改善基础设施，也在于建立更好的社会激励机制。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Safe driving habits are practices which people know they should follow but often don't.","cn":"安全驾驶习惯是人们知道自己应该遵守、却常常不去遵守的行为规范。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"Dangerous driving is not a fixed cultural trait, as some imagine.","cn":"危险驾驶并不是某些人所认为的那种固定的文化特征。"},{"sp":"Q22","en":"People respond to incentives, such as traffic laws that are actually enforced.","cn":"人们会对激励措施作出反应，例如真正得到执行的交通法规。"}],"questions":[{"q":"Where does most ocean plastic come from?","options":["Ships at sea","Rivers flowing from inland cities and farms","Volcanoes under the sea","Fishing boats only"],"answer":1,"explain":"原文说 Most of it does not come from ships. It flows down rivers from cities and farms far inland。"},{"q":"What are microplastics?","options":["Pieces smaller than five millimetres","A kind of sea animal","Large plastic bottles","Chemicals used on farms"],"answer":0,"explain":"原文说 tiny pieces called microplastics, which are smaller than five millimetres。"},{"q":"What do researchers suggest as the main solution?","options":["Cleaning the ocean surface","Better waste collection upstream","Banning all fishing","Building more ships"],"answer":1,"explain":"原文说 the answer lies upstream: better waste collection，答案在上游的垃圾收集环节。"}],"cloze":[{"text":"Sunlight and waves break the plastic into tiny pieces called ______.","answers":["microplastics"],"hint":"微塑料"},{"text":"Fish ______ these pieces for food.","answers":["mistake"],"hint":"误认为"},{"text":"The answer lies upstream: better waste ______.","answers":["collection"],"hint":"收集"}]},{"id":"cet4-2021-06-2","level":"CET4","exam":"2021_06_2","year":2021,"month":6,"set":2,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2021年6月 四级第2套 · 听力真题","source":"2021年6月 CET-4 第2套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2021/cet4-2021-06-set2.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"An 81-year-old man ended up in Germany by accident after trying to get from Newcastle, Great Britain, to Rome, Italy.","cn":"一位81岁的老人在试图从英国纽卡斯尔前往意大利罗马时意外到达了德国。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The old age pensioner was on a mission to see the Pope, who is head of the Catholic Church, and decided to make his way there by car.","cn":"这位领取养老金的老人此行是为了拜见天主教会领袖教皇,他决定驾车前往。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"He was surprised when his GPS system told him he had arrived, although there were no signs of any of the famous buildings or architecture.","cn":"当GPS系统告诉他已经到达目的地时,他感到很惊讶,因为周围没有任何著名建筑的迹象。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The man parked but didn't put on the handbrake of his car properly.","cn":"老人停好车,但没有正确拉上手刹。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"His car rolled backwards, and in a striking display of irony, hit a sign saying \"Rom\"—the small town in North Germany he had mistakenly plugged into the GPS system.","cn":"他的车向后滑行,极具讽刺意味的是,撞上了一块写着\"Rom\"的标志牌——这是他误输入GPS系统的德国北部小镇的名字。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Police said that the car had come to a halt after hitting the sign, but did not appear to be seriously damaged, although an ambulance was called to check on the pensioner.","cn":"警方表示,汽车撞上标志牌后停了下来,但似乎没有严重损坏,不过还是叫了救护车来检查这位老人的身体状况。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The man, who lives in the UK and is originally Italian, might have been confused by the fact that Rome is written \"Roma\" in Italian and \"Rom\" in German.","cn":"这位生活在英国、原籍意大利的老人可能是因为罗马在意大利语中写作\"Roma\",而在德语中写作\"Rom\"而产生了混淆。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Glasgow has pledged to become the first carbon neutral city in the UK.","cn":"Glasgow承诺成为英国首个碳中和城市。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The city's council and ScottishPower have announced a range of strategies in an attempt to reduce carbon emissions ahead of the new national target of 2045.","cn":"该市议会和ScottishPower宣布了一系列战略，试图在2045年这一新的国家目标之前减少碳排放。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"First Minister Nicola Sturgeon welcomed the pledge, and said: \"Today's announcement between ScottishPower and Glasgow City Council—to make Glasgow the UK's first net-zero city—is a very welcome step. Reaching our goals will need exactly this kind of partnership approach—with government, business, local authorities and citizens all playing their part.\"","cn":"首席大臣Nicola Sturgeon对这一承诺表示欢迎，并说：\"今天ScottishPower与Glasgow市议会之间的宣布——使Glasgow成为英国首个净零排放城市——是非常值得欢迎的一步。实现我们的目标需要正是这种伙伴关系方式——政府、企业、地方当局和公民都发挥各自的作用。\""},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Speaking ahead of the All Energy Conference being held in Glasgow, ScottishPower chief executive Keith Anderson said: \"We have a large supply of renewable energy on our doorstep and one of the only two low emission zones in action across the UK. Now, we need to invest in the technologies and programmes that transform the rest of Glasgow's economy and make us net zero before anyone else.\"","cn":"在Glasgow举行的全能源大会之前发言时,ScottishPower首席执行官Keith Anderson说：\"我们家门口有大量的可再生能源供应，并且拥有全英国仅有的两个低排放区之一。现在，我们需要投资于技术和项目，以转变Glasgow经济的其他部分，使我们比其他任何人都更早实现净零排放。\""},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"A Japanese IT firm has officially introduced an \"office cat\" policy to combat the stressful environment of the workplace.","cn":"一家日本IT公司正式推出了\"办公室猫\"政策,以应对压力重重的工作环境。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"A total of nine furry friends freely wander around in the office and do whatever their little hearts desire.","cn":"共有九只毛茸茸的朋友在办公室里自由走动,做着它们内心想做的任何事情。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Hidenobu Fukuda, who heads the firm, introduced the pet policy, upon request from one of his employees, allowing staff to bring their own cats to work.","cn":"公司负责人Hidenobu Fukuda应一位员工的要求推出了这项宠物政策,允许员工将自己的猫带到工作场所。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Employee Eri Ito is grateful for their animals' comforting ways. \"Cats are sleeping just beside us. It's healing.\" she said. Not only does Fukuda encourage bringing cats to the job, but he also encourages his employees to rescue cats from overpopulated shelters or streets. He gives 5,000 yen, about 45 US dollars a month to those who rescue a cat.","cn":"员工Eri Ito对这些动物带来的慰藉心怀感激。她说:\"猫就睡在我们身边,这很治愈。\"Fukuda不仅鼓励员工带猫上班,还鼓励员工从过度拥挤的收容所或街头救助猫。他每月向救助猫的员工提供5000日元,约合45美元。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"While the positives are many, there are still some obstacles. \"Sometimes a cat will walk on a phone and cut off the call, or they shut down the computers by walking onto the off switch,\" Ito says.","cn":"虽然好处很多,但仍存在一些障碍。Ito说:\"有时猫会走到电话上挂断通话,或者它们走到关机开关上把电脑关掉。\""},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Still, cats in the workplace have been a tremendous success for the company.","cn":"尽管如此,办公室里的猫对公司来说仍是一项巨大的成功。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The policy has led to various other companies doing the same.","cn":"这项政策促使其他多家公司也采取了同样的做法。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Has Jimmy been coming in lately?","cn":"M: Jimmy 最近有来吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: No, I haven't seen him around.","cn":"W: 没有，我没见他在附近。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Why?","cn":"怎么了？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Has he been causing any trouble?","cn":"他惹什么麻烦了吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Not that I know of.","cn":"M: 据我所知没有。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But I need to see him, because my friends and I lent him some money last month.","cn":"但我需要见他，因为上个月我和朋友们借了他一些钱。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"We haven't heard from him since.","cn":"从那以后就没他消息了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I heard he comes here a lot, so I thought I'd come in and check with you.","cn":"我听说他经常来这儿，所以想过来问问你。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Well, that's funny.","cn":"W: 嗯，这倒挺有意思。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Some other fellow came in asking for Jimmy just yesterday, a real nervous, pushy type of fellow, saying he needed Jimmy for some study project they were working on.","cn":"就在昨天还有个人来找 Jimmy，一个特别紧张、咄咄逼人的家伙，说他需要找 Jimmy 完成他们一起做的什么学习项目。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But I can't quite remember what it was all about.","cn":"但我记不太清具体是什么了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Is this a lot of money we're talking about here?","cn":"你们说的是一大笔钱吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: No, just 60 pounds between the three of us, but still a bit too much to just let go.","cn":"M: 不是，我们三个人一共就 60 英镑，但也不至于就这么算了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"He told us he'd got into an accident.","cn":"他告诉我们他出了个事故。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Nothing serious, mind you, but he damaged someone's car and wanted to get some money together to make up for the damage he'd caused.","cn":"不严重，你知道，但他撞坏了别人的车，想凑点钱赔偿他造成的损失。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Hmm, isn't that sort of thing usually covered by insurance?","cn":"W: 嗯，这种事不是通常都有保险赔吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"And then, if you still wanted to give money as some sort of apology or something, he probably shouldn't have to go around borrowing it from people.","cn":"而且就算你还想给钱作为某种道歉什么的，他也不应该到处找人借钱吧。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: You think Jimmy's just making it all up? See, I did think it was a bit weird for him to be asking for money for that sort of thing. And his story was a bit vague to begin with. But I thought maybe he doesn't want his parents to know about what happened. So he'd rather come to us and keep things quiet. Anyway, Jimmy is a good guy. So we didn't make a fuss about it.","cn":"M: 你觉得 Jimmy 是编出来的？你看，我当时确实觉得他为这种事要钱有点奇怪。而且他的说法一开始就挺含糊的。但我想也许他不想让父母知道发生了什么，所以宁愿来找我们，把事情压下来。不管怎样，Jimmy 是个好人，所以我们也没多计较。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Hi, Max. How are you? Listen. I wanted to ask you about ordering shopping online. I've never done it before and I know that you've been doing it for ages.","cn":"W: 嗨,Max。你好吗?听着,我想问你关于网上购物的事。我以前从来没试过,我知道你已经用了很久了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Sure.","cn":"M: 当然。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I love getting my shopping delivered.","cn":"我很喜欢送货上门。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It makes life so much simpler—no carrying heavy shopping bags in the rain, or trying to park the car on those huge supermarket car parks then not being able to find it again after you come out of the shops.","cn":"这让生活简单多了——不用在雨天提着沉重的购物袋,也不用在那些超大的超市停车场停车,然后从商店出来后又找不到自己的车。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: But there must be some problems.","cn":"W: 但肯定会有些问题吧。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I mean, how do you know that you won't get bad fruit, or that the eggs won't be broken?","cn":"我是说,你怎么知道不会买到坏水果,或者鸡蛋不会破呢?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Oh, come on.","cn":"M: 哦,别这样。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"The food is exactly the same as the stuff you buy in a conventional shop.","cn":"食物和你在传统商店买的东西完全一样。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"They aren't going to deliver you food that is out of date.","cn":"他们不会给你送过期的食品。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And if you get a broken egg, well, that could happen in a conventional shop, too.","cn":"如果你收到破损的鸡蛋,这在传统商店也可能发生。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"If anything is really wrong, you can just take photographs of the damage, and they will give you the money back or replace the item.","cn":"如果真的有什么问题,你可以拍下损坏的照片,他们会退钱或者换货。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: How about delivery fees? Is it not more expensive to get everything delivered?","cn":"W: 配送费怎么样?送货上门不是更贵吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: I actually found that it was cheaper for me, as I live quite far away from my local supermarket.","cn":"M: 实际上我发现对我来说更便宜,因为我住得离本地超市挺远的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So with the deliveries, I'm actually saving on petrol.","cn":"所以有了配送服务,我实际上还节省了汽油费。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I've never thought of that.","cn":"W: 我从没想过这一点。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"If you aren't driving your own car, then you are saving on fuel.","cn":"如果你不开自己的车,那就省了油钱。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Right, you've convinced me.","cn":"好吧,你说服我了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I'm going to go on the computer now and give it a try.","cn":"我现在就去电脑上试试。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So, which supermarket do you think is the best to order from?","cn":"那么,你觉得哪家超市最值得下单?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Oh, no.","cn":"M: 哦,不。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"That's definitely up to you.","cn":"那肯定要你自己决定。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Otherwise, we'll be here all day.","cn":"否则,我们得在这儿待一整天了。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"A recent study found that 10 percent of British children suffer from math anxiety.","cn":"最近一项研究发现,10%的英国儿童患有数学焦虑症。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"This means they have overwhelming negative emotions towards the subject, ranging from rage to despair.","cn":"这意味着他们对这门学科有压倒性的负面情绪,从愤怒到绝望不等。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Other emotions triggered by math include feelings of \"tension and frustration\".","cn":"数学引发的其他情绪还包括\"紧张和挫败感\"。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Physical symptoms include a racing heart or struggling to catch breath.","cn":"生理症状包括心跳加速或呼吸困难。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The phenomenon of math anxiety is characterized as a general sense of feeling that the subject is hard compared with other subjects leading to a subsequent lack or loss of confidence.","cn":"数学焦虑现象的特征是一种普遍的感觉,即认为这门学科比其他学科更难,从而导致信心不足或丧失信心。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Researchers said they investigated individuals' attitudes towards mathematics because of what could be referred to as a mathematics crisis in the UK.","cn":"研究人员表示,他们之所以调查个人对数学的态度,是因为英国可以称之为数学危机的现象。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"There's a widespread misunderstanding that only low performing children suffer from math anxiety.","cn":"人们普遍误解只有成绩差的儿童才会患有数学焦虑症。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"People automatically assume children are anxious about math because they are poor achievers.","cn":"人们自动认为儿童对数学感到焦虑是因为他们成绩不好。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"In fact, more than three quarters of children with high levels of math anxiety are normal to high achievers.","cn":"事实上,超过四分之三有高度数学焦虑的儿童是正常到高水平的成就者。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Probably their math anxiety will go unnoticed because their performance is good.","cn":"他们的数学焦虑可能不会被注意到,因为他们的成绩很好。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"But in the long term their performance is negatively affected.","cn":"但从长远来看,他们的表现会受到负面影响。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"So the real danger here is that children who will be completely able to do math at a normal level may keep away from it because they feel anxious.","cn":"所以真正的危险在于,完全有能力达到正常水平做数学的儿童可能会远离它,因为他们感到焦虑。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Math anxiety can severely disrupt students' performance in the subject in both primary and secondary school.","cn":"数学焦虑会严重扰乱学生在小学和中学阶段这门学科的表现。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"But importantly—and surprisingly—this new study suggests that the majority of students experiencing math anxiety have normal to high math ability.","cn":"但重要的是——也令人惊讶的是——这项新研究表明,大多数经历数学焦虑的学生具有正常到较高的数学能力。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"People spend a lot of time using phones and computers.","cn":"人们花费大量时间使用手机和电脑。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Much of that time is devoted to text messages and social media.","cn":"这些时间大部分用于发送短信和使用社交媒体。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But many people choose to spend their time playing computer games.","cn":"但许多人选择把时间花在玩电脑游戏上。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"For years, parents and teachers have worried that these games might be addictive.","cn":"多年来,家长和教师一直担心这些游戏可能会让人上瘾。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"And now, the World Health Organization has recognized addiction to computer games as a disease.","cn":"现在,世界卫生组织已经将电脑游戏成瘾认定为一种疾病。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The organization explains that this decision reflects general agreement among experts around the world that some people have a problem with these games.","cn":"该组织解释说,这一决定反映了全球专家的普遍共识,即有些人在这些游戏上存在问题。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"They show a pattern of behavior characterized by a lack of control.","cn":"他们表现出以缺乏控制力为特征的行为模式。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Such people make computer games a priority over their responsibilities.","cn":"这些人将电脑游戏置于自己的责任之上。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"They may play games instead of attending school, or work, or socializing.","cn":"他们可能不去上学、不去工作或不参加社交活动,而是玩游戏。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"According to the World Health Organization experts, people's use of computer games is different from their use of the Internet, social media and online shopping.","cn":"根据世界卫生组织专家的说法,人们对电脑游戏的使用不同于他们对互联网、社交媒体和网上购物的使用。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"These experts claim there is not sufficient data to indicate that people's reliance on those other activities is an addiction.","cn":"这些专家声称,没有足够的数据表明人们对其他这些活动的依赖是一种成瘾。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But they argue that playing computer games to access is different.","cn":"但他们认为,为了获取而玩电脑游戏是不同的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"This behavior can become a disorder.","cn":"这种行为可能成为一种障碍。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"To meet the new definition for addiction, the behavior must damage a person's relationships or performance at school or work, and this must last for at least a year.","cn":"要符合成瘾的新定义,这种行为必须损害一个人的人际关系或在学校或工作中的表现,并且这种情况必须持续至少一年。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Still not all behavior experts agree.","cn":"但并非所有行为专家都同意这一观点。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Some argue that there's not enough research on the subject.","cn":"一些人认为关于这个主题的研究还不够充分。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Thus, they claim it is too early to call computer game addiction a disorder.","cn":"因此,他们声称现在将电脑游戏成瘾称为一种障碍还为时过早。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Maybe you carry the most powerful passport in the world, or perhaps the rarest passport.","cn":"也许你持有世界上最强大的护照,或者可能是最稀有的护照。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Whatever the case, your passport will likely be one of four colors: red, blue, green or black, although there are slight variations.","cn":"无论如何,你的护照很可能是四种颜色之一:红色、蓝色、绿色或黑色,尽管存在细微的差异。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Switzerland's passport is dark red, for example, while most European countries prefer a shade of red.","cn":"例如,瑞士的护照是深红色,而大多数欧洲国家更喜欢红色的色调。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"That's almost brown.","cn":"那几乎是棕色的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"There are no official rules regarding passport colors, but countries follow a certain set of norms when designing them.","cn":"关于护照颜色没有官方规定,但各国在设计护照时遵循一套特定的规范。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The International Civil Aviation Organization, which works to define the principles of air travel, suggests that countries use a suitable type, size and style for official documents like passports.","cn":"国际民用航空组织致力于定义航空旅行的原则,建议各国为护照等官方文件使用合适的类型、尺寸和样式。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"There are also a few compulsory aspects of passports.","cn":"护照还有一些强制性要求。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"They must be made from a material that bends.","cn":"护照必须由可弯曲的材料制成。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"They should be able to be read by a machine at temperatures ranging from 10 degrees Celsius to 50 degrees Celsius, under the conditions where the air can be extremely dry or moist.","cn":"它们应当能够在10摄氏度到50摄氏度的温度范围内被机器读取,在空气可能极度干燥或潮湿的条件下。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Despite these existing recommendations, there is nothing regarding the cover color. Why? Simply put, countries stick to darker and more conservative colors because they appear more official. And they can also hide dirt and wear. While there's little innovation when it comes to passport cover color, the same cannot be said for the pages. The passports of many countries can take images of their well-known geographical features and wildlife, which also function as security features as some are only visible under a special light.","cn":"尽管存在这些现行建议,但没有关于封面颜色的规定。为什么?简单来说,各国坚持使用更深、更保守的颜色,因为它们看起来更正式。而且它们还可以隐藏污垢和磨损。虽然在护照封面颜色方面几乎没有创新,但在内页方面却并非如此。许多国家的护照可以采用其著名地理特征和野生动物的图像,这些图像也具有安全功能,因为有些图像只有在特殊光线下才能看到。"}]},{"id":"cet4-2021-12-1","level":"CET4","exam":"2021_12_1","year":2021,"month":12,"set":1,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2021年12月 四级第1套 · 听力真题","source":"2021年12月 CET-4 第1套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2021/cet4-2021-12-set1.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"United Airlines has apologised for mistakenly shipping an American family's pet dog thousands of miles in the wrong direction to Japan.","cn":"美国联合航空公司为误将一个美国家庭的宠物狗运送到数千英里外的日本方向而道歉。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The dog owner's beloved 10-year-old dog named Buddy took an unexpected 16-hour flight to Tokyo following a mix-up by the airline.","cn":"狗主人心爱的10岁狗狗名叫Buddy,由于航空公司的失误,意外搭乘了16小时的航班飞往东京。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The dog owner's family are currently in the process of moving.","cn":"狗主人一家目前正在搬家过程中。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"They were meant to be reunited with the pet in their new home city in Texas.","cn":"他们原本应该在得克萨斯州的新家与宠物团聚。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"But when they arrived at the United Airlines cargo facility in the southern U.S. state, they found a stranger's dog waiting in Buddy's place.","cn":"但当他们到达美国南部州的美国联合航空公司货运设施时,发现一只陌生的狗在Buddy的位置等待。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Both of the dogs had been sent to the wrong destinations on connecting flights from Denver, with Buddy mistakenly being sent to Japan instead.","cn":"这两只狗都在丹佛转机时被送到了错误的目的地,Buddy被错误地送到了日本。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Buddy was given a physical checkup when he arrived at Tokyo's International Airport.","cn":"Buddy抵达东京国际机场后接受了身体检查。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The dog was then sent back to the U.S. on a private charter jet.","cn":"随后这只狗被用私人包机送回美国。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"\"I'm so glad he's alive and coming home soon!\" said the relieved dog owner.","cn":"\"我太高兴了,它还活着并且很快就要回家了!\"如释重负的狗主人说。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"\"And an error occurred during the connections in Denver. We have notified our customers that their pets arrived safely. We will arrange to return the pets to them as soon as possible,\" a spokesperson of United Airlines said.","cn":"\"在丹佛转机期间发生了一个错误。我们已通知客户他们的宠物安全抵达。我们将尽快安排将宠物送还给他们。\"美国联合航空公司发言人表示。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Officials at Reid Park Zoo in Tucson Arizona are celebrating the birth of a baby elephant.","cn":"亚利桑那州图森市Reid Park动物园的官员们正在庆祝一头小象的诞生。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Zoo officials say the baby was born on Monday.","cn":"动物园官员表示,这头小象于周一出生。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"It is a female and she weighs nearly 130 kilograms.","cn":"它是雌性,体重近130公斤。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Semba, her mother, is a 30-year-old African elephant.","cn":"它的母亲Semba是一头30岁的非洲象。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The pregnancy lasted 22 months.","cn":"怀孕期持续了22个月。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Officials describe the baby elephant as \"healthy, standing and nursing\".","cn":"官员们描述这头小象\"健康、能站立并在哺乳\"。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The baby hasn't been given a name yet.","cn":"这头小象还没有被命名。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Semba has given birth before.","cn":"Semba之前曾生育过。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Zoo officials said during this pregnancy, she was closely monitored through physical exams and blood tests.","cn":"动物园官员表示,在这次怀孕期间,通过身体检查和血液测试对她进行了密切监测。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Dr. Sue Tygielski is the zoo's director of zoological operations.","cn":"Sue Tygielski博士是该动物园的动物运营总监。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"She said the elephant's birth went smoothly and that there were no complications.","cn":"她表示大象的分娩过程顺利,没有出现并发症。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The new baby expands the zoo's elephant herd to six.","cn":"这头新生小象使动物园的大象群扩大到六头。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"That includes the baby's parents, a sister, a brother and an adult female.","cn":"其中包括小象的父母、一个姐姐、一个哥哥和一头成年雌象。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Three years ago, a couple was enjoying a meal at a beach restaurant.","cn":"三年前,一对夫妇在一家海滩餐厅用餐。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The restaurant was built on a wooden structure above the sea-water.","cn":"这家餐厅建在海面上的木质结构上。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"During the meal, the man's wedding ring slipped off his finger.","cn":"用餐期间,男士的结婚戒指从手指上滑落了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"It fell through the wooden floorboards, apparently lost forever.","cn":"它掉进了木地板的缝隙里,看似永远丢失了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Recently, the restaurant manager Ryan Krivoy decided to replace the wooden deck and he found an old gold coin, some $100 bills and a silver wedding ring while replacing the deck.","cn":"最近,餐厅经理Ryan Krivoy决定更换木质甲板,在更换甲板时他发现了一枚古老的金币、一些100美元的钞票和一枚银质结婚戒指。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The restaurant waitress Sasha Formica posted a picture of the ring on Facebook.","cn":"餐厅女服务员Sasha Formica在Facebook上发布了这枚戒指的照片。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The post was shared about 5,000 times.","cn":"这条帖子被分享了大约5000次。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Three days later, the happy wife called to claim the ring.","cn":"三天后,这位高兴的妻子打电话来认领戒指。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"She even texted pictures of her and her husband eating there in 2017 as proof.","cn":"她甚至发送了她和丈夫2017年在那里用餐的照片作为证明。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The restaurant mailed the ring back to the happy couple.","cn":"餐厅将戒指邮寄回给了这对幸福的夫妇。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Meanwhile, Krivoy discovered that the gold coin was very rare.","cn":"与此同时,Krivoy发现那枚金币非常罕见。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"It was from 1855 and worth as much as $2,000.","cn":"它来自1855年,价值高达2000美元。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I can't believe that duck hunting is still legal in so many parts of the world.","cn":"W: 我真不敢相信在世界上这么多地方猎鸭仍然是合法的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"The scientific evidence from countries like Australia, Canada and the USA clearly indicates a decline in the birds' numbers.","cn":"来自澳大利亚、加拿大和美国等国家的科学证据清楚地表明这些鸟类的数量正在下降。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: But can anyone be sure if the decline is really caused by the hunting or by climate change?","cn":"M: 但是有人能确定这种下降真的是由狩猎引起的还是由气候变化引起的吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: It's caused by both in fact.","cn":"W: 实际上两者都有影响。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"We see more droughts in countries like Australia.","cn":"我们在澳大利亚这样的国家看到更多的干旱。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Ducks are birds that feed and breed in areas where there is a lot of water, but their habitats have been shrinking in recent decades because of the droughts.","cn":"鸭子是在有大量水源的地区觅食和繁殖的鸟类,但近几十年来由于干旱,它们的栖息地一直在缩小。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: And I guess with fewer places to inhabit, they concentrate in greater numbers in few areas, which surely makes them easier targets for the hunters.","cn":"M: 我猜随着可居住的地方越来越少,它们会更集中地聚集在少数几个区域,这肯定让它们更容易成为猎人的目标。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: It does.","cn":"W: 确实如此。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"My grandfather was a duck hunter.","cn":"我祖父曾是个猎鸭人。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"He told me hunting ducks and geese began in the 19th century.","cn":"他告诉我猎鸭和猎鹅始于19世纪。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"They were easily found and a plentifully available food source in farming areas, especially for poor immigrants.","cn":"在农业地区它们很容易找到,是充足的食物来源,尤其对贫穷的移民来说。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: What do they use for hunting during that period?","cn":"M: 那个时期他们用什么来狩猎?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: They use new types of guns, and birds could easily be shot down in flight.","cn":"W: 他们使用新型枪支,鸟类在飞行中很容易被射下来。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"And in such great numbers, their commercial hunting of ducks and geese became an industry.","cn":"而且数量如此之多,对鸭子和鹅的商业狩猎成了一个产业。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Yet, there's no commercial farming of these birds nowadays.","cn":"然而,现在已经没有这些鸟类的商业养殖了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Their meat is hardly eaten in Western countries.","cn":"在西方国家几乎没人吃它们的肉。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: No, duck hunting seemingly exists as the continuation of a tradition.","cn":"M: 是的,猎鸭似乎只是作为一种传统的延续而存在。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Well, ducks have never been popular with farmers like my grandfather anyway because they sometimes destroy crops.","cn":"W: 其实,鸭子从来都不受像我祖父这样的农民欢迎,因为它们有时会破坏庄稼。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"In fact, farmers used to poison them in large numbers.","cn":"事实上,农民过去常常大量毒杀它们。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: That somehow doesn't surprise me.","cn":"M: 这倒不让我意外。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Nobody places much value on the lives of these poor birds or on their meat.","cn":"没人重视这些可怜鸟儿的生命,也不重视它们的肉。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Okay, Miss Bright.","cn":"M: 好的，Bright小姐。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I've finished calculating.","cn":"我已经算完了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I estimate you have between 210 and 240 square meters of walls and ceiling.","cn":"我估计您的墙面和天花板加起来有210到240平方米。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: So, how much would the paint job cost?","cn":"W: 那么，刷漆要花多少钱？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: That would depend on the quality of paint you choose.","cn":"M: 这取决于您选择的油漆质量。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"We carry two brands.","cn":"我们有两个品牌。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"One costs 60 cents every square meter, and the other 90 cents.","cn":"一种每平方米60美分，另一种90美分。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"The second is guaranteed to look great for about 10 years, whereas the cheaper one will start to dull after around six or seven years.","cn":"第二种保证能保持大约10年的良好效果，而便宜的那种在六七年后就会开始褪色。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: In that case, we would prefer the more expensive option.","cn":"W: 那样的话，我们更倾向于选贵一点的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: All right, then.","cn":"M: 好的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So including labor costs, taxes, and everything, this job would come to $3,000.","cn":"那么包括人工费、税费和所有费用，这项工作总共需要3000美元。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Um, to be perfectly honest, that's more than I expected.","cn":"W: 嗯，说实话，这比我预期的要高。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Please bear in mind that the price includes moving all the furniture, and the whole task would take two days.","cn":"M: 请注意价格包括搬动所有家具，而且整个任务需要两天时间。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Really? Why?","cn":"W: 真的吗?为什么？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Well, we can't paint the walls without clearing all the furniture first.","cn":"M: 嗯，我们不清空家具就没法刷墙。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So every time we paint a room, we first have to move the furniture to another room.","cn":"所以每刷一个房间，我们都得先把家具搬到另一个房间。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So that takes more time.","cn":"这样就需要更多时间。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Plus, it requires two people, which works out more expensive.","cn":"而且需要两个人，费用就更高了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I see.","cn":"W: 我明白了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"But does that mean I could not live here in my own house during those two days?","cn":"但这是不是意味着这两天我不能住在自己家里？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: That is correct.","cn":"M: 没错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Oh well, that changes everything, I'm afraid.","cn":"W: 哦，那恐怕一切都变了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I would have to stay with a friend or check into a hotel.","cn":"我得去朋友家住或者住酒店。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I hadn't considered any of that.","cn":"我之前都没考虑过这些。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I'm starting to realize that painting my house is far more troublesome than I had anticipated.","cn":"我开始意识到粉刷房子比我想象的麻烦得多。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: This is usually the case.","cn":"M: 通常都是这样。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Most of our clients go through the same realization.","cn":"我们大多数客户都会有同样的感受。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I see.","cn":"W: 明白了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: You have my number.","cn":"M: 您有我的电话。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Please feel free to call me for any further questions.","cn":"如果有任何其他问题，请随时给我打电话。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Thank you.","cn":"W: 谢谢。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Homework is an important part of schooling, but the purposes of giving children homework will change as they grow older.","cn":"家庭作业是学校教育的重要组成部分,但给孩子布置作业的目的会随着他们年龄的增长而改变。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"At the primary level, the main aim is to cultivate good habits, like learning to plan and exercising self-discipline.","cn":"在小学阶段,主要目的是培养良好的习惯,比如学会计划和锻炼自律。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"During the secondary school years, extending what is learned at school is positively related to academic achievement, so the content of homework becomes more important.","cn":"在中学阶段,拓展在学校学到的知识与学业成绩呈正相关,因此作业的内容变得更加重要。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"So how can you help your child do their best?","cn":"那么你如何帮助孩子做到最好呢?"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Creating an ideal working environment will make it easier for them to get down to their assignments quickly.","cn":"创造一个理想的学习环境会让他们更容易快速投入作业。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Make sure it's free of distractions, and for primary school children at least somewhere near you, so you can answer questions and offer encouragement.","cn":"确保环境没有干扰,至少对小学生来说要在你附近的某个地方,这样你就能回答问题并给予鼓励。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"You probably have to help younger children plan their session, but it's important that by the end of primary school it's second nature. Get them to tell you everything they have to do. Then encourage them to establish an order in which they do work.","cn":"你可能需要帮助年幼的孩子规划他们的学习时段,但重要的是到小学毕业时这应该成为自然而然的事情。让他们告诉你所有需要做的事情,然后鼓励他们确定完成作业的顺序。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"When there are several different assignments, make sure they begin with one they enjoy, so it seems easy to get started.","cn":"当有几项不同的作业时,确保他们从喜欢的作业开始,这样看起来容易上手。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"It's best to take on the most difficult task second once they're settled, but before they get tired.","cn":"最好在他们进入状态后、但还没感到疲倦之前,第二个处理最难的任务。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"If older children have more than an hour of homework, encourage them to schedule a short break to stretch.","cn":"如果年龄较大的孩子有超过一小时的作业,鼓励他们安排一个短暂的休息时间来伸展身体。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"If you encourage them to tell you what they've learned, they'll absorb the information more deeply and remember it more readily.","cn":"如果你鼓励他们告诉你学到了什么,他们会更深入地吸收信息并更容易记住它。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Workers at Mexican oil company will receive a healthy incentive of almost $300 a year if they meet certain body weight standards.","cn":"墨西哥石油公司的员工如果达到特定体重标准，将获得每年近300美元的丰厚奖励。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"To qualify for the bonus, they must maintain a healthy weight.","cn":"要获得这项奖金，他们必须保持健康体重。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"For those who are overweight or obese, they could receive the bonus if they reduce their weight by 10% during the year.","cn":"对于超重或肥胖的员工,如果在一年内减重10%,也可以获得该奖金。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Some applaud the policy as fair, because it rewards both the individuals who maintain a healthy weight and those who are working towards achieving it.","cn":"一些人赞扬这项政策公平合理,因为它既奖励保持健康体重的个人,也奖励那些正在努力实现这一目标的人。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But critics say the policy contradicts recommendations by many health experts, who warn that a person's weight is influenced by genetic and environmental factors.","cn":"但批评者表示,这项政策与许多健康专家的建议相矛盾,这些专家警告说,一个人的体重受遗传和环境因素的影响。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"That means weight can be hard for individuals to control, which makes the bonus unfair.","cn":"这意味着体重对个人来说很难控制,这使得这项奖金不公平。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Some experts say the policy is inconsistent with the science of what we know about body weight regulation.","cn":"一些专家表示,这项政策与我们关于体重调节的科学知识不一致。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"These experts argue that focusing on wage is the wrong approach.","cn":"这些专家认为,关注体重是错误的方法。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"A more productive method of encouraging health among employees is to promote healthy behaviors.","cn":"鼓励员工健康的更有效方法是促进健康行为。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"For example, companies can give workers gym memberships, or encourage participation in lectures on healthy eating and living.","cn":"例如,公司可以为员工提供健身房会员资格,或鼓励参加有关健康饮食和生活的讲座。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"They can also reduce sweets and provide healthier snacks in the office and healthier meals at the company canteen.","cn":"他们还可以减少甜食,在办公室提供更健康的零食,在公司食堂提供更健康的餐食。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Or they can give employees more time during their lunch break to exercise.","cn":"或者他们可以在午休时间给员工更多时间锻炼。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"These are much better and much more productive ways for companies to move forward on their employees' wellbeing.","cn":"这些都是公司在员工福祉方面前进的更好、更有效的方式。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Campaigners have warned that the British government is not doing enough to prevent left-handed pupils from falling behind their peers.","cn":"活动人士警告称,英国政府在防止左撇子学生落后于同龄人方面做得不够。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"They claim that thousands of children are still being \"penalized\" for being left-handed.","cn":"他们声称,成千上万的儿童仍因左撇子而受到\"惩罚\"。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"This is due to a lack of action from ministers, who've failed to take any meaningful action for years.","cn":"这是由于部长们缺乏行动,多年来未能采取任何有意义的措施。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"It is feared that a failure to address early-year challenges, such as poor handwriting, leads to much more serious problems down the line—with these pupils facing reduced career prospects.","cn":"人们担心,如果不能解决早期阶段的挑战,例如书写能力差,会导致后续出现更严重的问题——这些学生将面临职业前景受限的困境。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Studies in recent years show that left-handed children are more likely to suffer with learning difficulties and their scores are lower on IQ tests.","cn":"近年来的研究表明,左撇子儿童更容易出现学习困难,他们在智商测试中的得分也较低。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Campaigners feel it's strange that children in British schools are penalized because they happen to be left-handed.","cn":"活动人士认为奇怪的是,英国学校的儿童会因为恰好是左撇子而受到惩罚。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"They don't understand why successive governments have failed to act on this.","cn":"他们不理解为什么历届政府都未能就此采取行动。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"They want the department of education to record which children are left-handed and what their educational attainments are, since they make up some 10% of the population.","cn":"他们希望教育部记录哪些儿童是左撇子以及他们的学业成绩如何,因为左撇子占人口的约10%。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"In early-year education, left-handed children are struggling and making a mess of their handwriting.","cn":"在早期教育中,左撇子儿童很吃力,把字写得一团糟。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Educators don't know how to deal with this.","cn":"教育工作者不知道如何应对这一问题。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"In many cases, there is no active help and a lack of teacher training.","cn":"在许多情况下,没有积极的帮助,也缺乏教师培训。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Campaigners point out that a high percentage of the prison population is left-handed.","cn":"活动人士指出,监狱人口中左撇子的比例很高。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"They say that these prison numbers are unusually high and ask why it is the case.","cn":"他们说这些监狱数字异常高,并询问为什么会出现这种情况。"}]},{"id":"cet4-2021-12-2","level":"CET4","exam":"2021_12_2","year":2021,"month":12,"set":2,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2021年12月 四级第2套 · 听力真题","source":"2021年12月 CET-4 第2套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2021/cet4-2021-12-set2.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"A 22-year-old Chinese woman who suffered from a persistent cough was shocked to learn that she had a piece of chicken bone lodged in her lung.","cn":"一名22岁的中国女性因持续咳嗽而震惊地得知,她的肺部卡着一块鸡骨头。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The unnamed woman, from the province of Shandong, started to have coughing problems when she was 7 or 8 years old.","cn":"这名来自山东省的未透露姓名的女性,在7岁或8岁时开始出现咳嗽问题。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"For 14 years, she made numerous hospital visits.","cn":"14年来,她多次前往医院就诊。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"However, no doctor could identify any problem.","cn":"然而,没有一位医生能够发现任何问题。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Her uncontrollable coughing was a mystery.","cn":"她无法控制的咳嗽一直是个谜。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Finally, the woman got a full body scan at a hospital in the city of Qingdao.","cn":"最终,这名女性在青岛市的一家医院进行了全身扫描。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"This special medical procedure revealed she had a chicken bone stuck in her lung.","cn":"这项特殊的医疗检查显示她的肺部卡着一块鸡骨头。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"Doctors performed surgery and removed the bone.","cn":"医生进行了手术并取出了骨头。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"The simple procedure went smoothly and the woman has recovered fully.","cn":"这个简单的手术进行得很顺利,女性已完全康复。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 1","en":"With the bone finally removed from her lung, the woman is very happy that she no longer suffers from that annoying cough.","cn":"随着骨头最终从肺部取出,这名女性非常高兴,因为她不再遭受那恼人的咳嗽困扰。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"A white sheep named Prickles that ran away from an Australian farm during the 2013 bushfires, recently returned home.","cn":"一只名叫Prickles的白羊在2013年丛林大火期间从澳大利亚一个农场逃跑,最近回家了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"According to farmer Alice Gray, Prickles was only a lamb when she ran away.","cn":"据农场主Alice Gray说,Prickles逃跑时还只是一只羊羔。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"The bushfires that hit the area back then destroyed a large part of her family's massive property.","cn":"当时袭击该地区的丛林大火摧毁了她家大片地产的很大一部分。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"They thought Prickles had died in the fire.","cn":"他们以为Prickles在火灾中丧生了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"But instead, the young sheep escaped into a 200-acre forest near the farm.","cn":"但实际上,这只小羊逃进了农场附近一片200英亩的森林。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Once the fires were over, the family had to fix the damage done to the farm, as it was such a large property.","cn":"火灾结束后,由于地产面积很大,这家人不得不修复农场遭受的损坏。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"This included rebuilding about 50 kilometers of fencing.","cn":"这包括重建约50公里的围栏。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"It was this huge fencing that prevented Prickles from finding her way back.","cn":"正是这道巨大的围栏阻止了Prickles找到回家的路。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Over the years, the family spotted her a few times.","cn":"多年来,这家人看到过她几次。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"They even recorded her with cameras installed to monitor deer activity.","cn":"他们甚至用安装来监测鹿类活动的相机拍到过她。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"But while they knew Prickles was alive, they couldn't find her and never expected her to return by herself.","cn":"但尽管他们知道Prickles还活着,却找不到她,也从未料到她会自己回来。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 2","en":"Seven years later, they were proven wrong.","cn":"七年后,事实证明他们错了。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Tons of gold have fallen out of the sky in Russia after a cargo plane malfunctioned in midair this morning.","cn":"今天上午，一架货机在空中发生故障后，数吨黄金从俄罗斯天空坠落。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The aircraft was carrying 265 million pounds worth of gold and diamonds, when the door flew open—sending the precious metal back to earth.","cn":"这架飞机载有价值2.65亿英镑的黄金和钻石，当舱门突然打开时，贵重金属被抛回地面。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"According to the official news agency, Russian authorities have recovered more than 170 gold bars weighing 20 kilograms each.","cn":"据官方通讯社报道，俄罗斯当局已经回收了超过170根金条，每根重20公斤。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"The plane was traveling from Yakutsk Airport in a major diamond-producing region to the city Krasnoyarsk in Siberia.","cn":"该飞机从主要钻石产区的Yakutsk机场飞往西伯利亚的Krasnoyarsk市。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"However, the aircraft made an emergency landing in Magan after it began losing some of its valuable cargo.","cn":"然而，这架飞机在开始丢失部分贵重货物后，在Magan紧急降落。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Reports suggest some bars of gold were scattered up to 15 miles away from the airport.","cn":"报道称，一些金条散落在距离机场15英里远的地方。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Nine tons of gold on plane AN-12 belonged to a goldmine company.","cn":"AN-12飞机上的9吨黄金属于一家金矿公司。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Police have sealed off the runway, and say it is unclear if it was an accident or an attempted robbery.","cn":"警方已经封锁了跑道，并表示尚不清楚这是一起事故还是抢劫未遂。"},{"sp":"短篇新闻 3","en":"Technical engineers who worked on the plane prior to take-off are reportedly going to be questioned by the police.","cn":"据报道，起飞前在飞机上工作的技术工程师将接受警方问询。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Hello, you're through to customer service.","cn":"M: 您好,您已接通客户服务部。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"This is Michael speaking.","cn":"我是Michael。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Before we continue, I just want to make you aware that this call is being recorded and may be used in the future for training purposes.","cn":"在我们继续之前,我想提醒您,本通话正在录音,未来可能用于培训目的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"What can I help you with today?","cn":"请问有什么可以帮您的?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Hi, my name is Jean Seimon.","cn":"W: 您好,我叫Jean Seimon。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I recently bought an office chair from your company, but I returned it about a week ago.","cn":"我最近从贵公司买了一把办公椅,但大约一周前退了货。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I'm just calling to inquire when I will be able to get my money back.","cn":"我打电话是想询问什么时候能拿到退款。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It says on your website that your company will pay back the money within three working days of you receiving the returned item.","cn":"贵公司网站上说,在收到退货后三个工作日内会退款。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But it's been five working days and I haven't received anything.","cn":"但已经过了五个工作日了,我还没收到任何款项。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I'm sorry to hear that, Miss Seimon.","cn":"M: 很抱歉听到这个情况,Seimon女士。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"What's your customer reference number, please?","cn":"请问您的客户编号是多少?"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: It's 389460.","cn":"W: 是389460。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Okay, 389460.","cn":"M: 好的,389460。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I'm just looking on the system here.","cn":"我这就在系统里查一下。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"And according to our records, the chair you returned was received by our warehouse on Friday morning.","cn":"根据我们的记录,您退回的椅子是周五上午被我们仓库收到的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"The payment was made on Wednesday.","cn":"退款是在周三处理的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But this seems to be a problem with your card number.","cn":"但您的卡号似乎有问题。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: My card number? Oh, maybe it has something to do with my new card. It was sent to me on Tuesday. Maybe the bank canceled my old one before you've made the payment.","cn":"W: 我的卡号?哦,可能跟我的新卡有关。周二才寄给我的。也许银行在你们付款之前把我的旧卡注销了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Well, you'll need to update your card details directly on our website. Just make sure you're logged in. And then under the description of your personal information, you should see an option for updating payment methods.","cn":"M: 那您需要直接在我们网站上更新您的银行卡信息。确保您已经登录,然后在个人信息栏下面,应该能看到更新付款方式的选项。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I am logged in, and I'll give that a go.","cn":"W: 我已经登录了,我试试看。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: I'll make a note here on the system for you, so that the payment will be made tomorrow morning.","cn":"M: 我会在系统里给您做个备注,这样明天上午就能给您退款。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Thank you very much.","cn":"W: 非常感谢。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: I'm getting a bit hungry.","cn":"M: 我有点饿了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Yes, me too.","cn":"W: 是啊,我也是。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I'm starving.","cn":"我快饿死了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Are you going to prepare a meal for us?","cn":"你要给我们做饭吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: No, sorry, I'm actually pretty worn out.","cn":"M: 不,抱歉,我实在太累了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Let's just go out somewhere close to eat.","cn":"我们还是出去找个近点的地方吃吧。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Well, I think we should stay in and save some cash.","cn":"W: 嗯,我觉得我们应该待在家里省点钱。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Can we get a meal delivered?","cn":"我们可以叫外卖吗?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Yeah, great.","cn":"M: 好啊,太好了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I'll use that food delivery app on my phone.","cn":"我用手机上的外卖app点。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"What do you want, fried chicken, hamburgers, or fish and chips?","cn":"你想吃什么,炸鸡、汉堡还是炸鱼薯条?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Oh, can we stay away from the junk food? How about something healthy?","cn":"W: 哦,我们能不能别吃垃圾食品?来点健康的怎么样?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Okay, well, there's a place that does salads.","cn":"M: 好吧,有家店做沙拉的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Let me have a look at that.","cn":"W: 让我看看。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Yeah, that looks delicious.","cn":"嗯,看起来挺好吃的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"But to be honest, I'd prefer something hot, not cold.","cn":"但说实话,我更想吃点热的,不要凉的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: How about Indian food?","cn":"M: 印度菜怎么样?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: That's not the kind of hot I mean. I'm just not a fan of sauces. That made me sweat and cry. I need something mild.","cn":"W: 我说的热不是那种辣。我就是不喜欢那种酱料,会让我出汗流泪。我要清淡点的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Okay. So would you consider Mexican? Oh no, sorry. There's also very hot pepper in that. Would you like some Italian food, perhaps? It's a bit heavy, but it's great food for a cold night like this.","cn":"M: 好的。那你会考虑墨西哥菜吗?哦不,抱歉。那里面也有很辣的辣椒。那意大利菜怎么样?有点油腻,但在这么冷的晚上吃很不错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Pizza? Spaghetti with creamy sauce? I know it's really tasty and great comfort food, but it's too fattening for me. I'm trying to keep a slim figure, you know.","cn":"W: 披萨?奶油酱意大利面?我知道真的很好吃,是很棒的comfort food,但对我来说太容易发胖了。你知道的,我想保持苗条身材。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Oh, you're really difficult to please.","cn":"M: 哦,你真是太难伺候了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Well, there's a nice Chinese restaurant that delivers.","cn":"嗯,有家不错的中餐馆可以送外卖。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Yes, I love Chinese food.","cn":"W: 好啊,我喜欢中国菜。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Let me see.","cn":"让我看看。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Oh, it's 15 kilometers away.","cn":"哦,有15公里远。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: That's a bit too far away.","cn":"M: 那有点太远了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Do you feel like Vietnamese food then?","cn":"那越南菜你觉得怎么样?"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Yeah, awesome.","cn":"W: 好啊,太棒了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It's healthy, and we can afford it.","cn":"健康,而且我们也吃得起。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Great.","cn":"M: 太好了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Let's order Vietnamese right away.","cn":"我们马上点越南菜吧。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"A new study carried out by the University of Lincoln has found a link between the personalities of cat owners and the behaviour and wellbeing of their cats.","cn":"林肯大学开展的一项新研究发现,猫主人的性格与其猫的行为和健康状况之间存在联系。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The findings suggest that, just as a parent's personality can affect the personality of a child, the same is true for a cat and its owner.","cn":"研究结果表明,正如父母的性格会影响孩子的性格一样,猫和其主人之间也是如此。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Owners—defined as individuals with high levels of anxiety, fear, anger, depression and loneliness—were more likely to have cats with behavioural issues.","cn":"那些被定义为具有高度焦虑、恐惧、愤怒、抑郁和孤独感的主人,更有可能养出有行为问题的猫。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Such cats displayed more aggressive and anxious behavioural styles as well as more stress-related sickness.","cn":"这些猫表现出更具攻击性和焦虑的行为方式,以及更多与压力相关的疾病。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"They were also more likely to have an ongoing medical condition and be overweight.","cn":"它们也更有可能患有持续性疾病和超重。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The research also found that mentally well-adjusted owners had calmer, happier and healthier cats.","cn":"研究还发现,心理健康状况良好的主人养的猫更平静、更快乐、更健康。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The researchers explained that \"Many owners regard their pets as a family member, and form close social bonds with them.\" The majority of owners want to provide the best care for their pets and it's therefore possible that pets could be affected by the way their owners interact with and manage them. The study highlights an important relationship between our personalities and the wellbeing of our pets. Further research is needed to investigate the causal nature of this relationship and to look at how owners' personalities are directly influencing their pets' behaviour and wellbeing.","cn":"研究人员解释说,\"许多主人将他们的宠物视为家庭成员,并与它们建立了紧密的社会联系。\"大多数主人希望为他们的宠物提供最好的照顾,因此宠物可能会受到主人与它们互动和管理方式的影响。这项研究强调了我们的性格与宠物健康之间的重要关系。需要进一步研究来探讨这种关系的因果性质,以及主人的性格如何直接影响宠物的行为和健康状况。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"It is possible that the wellbeing of pets is driven by the underlying nature of the owner, not simply by their conscious decisions and behaviours.","cn":"宠物的健康状况可能是由主人的内在本质驱动的,而不仅仅是由他们有意识的决定和行为驱动的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"\"One 60-minute run can add seven hours to your life.\" This was a claim made by The Times last week. The claim was based on a new review of studies about the effects of running. The review concluded that on average runners live three years longer than non-runners and that running does more to extend life than any other form of exercise. But there's more to running than its health benefits. Research published in recent years has shown that running changes your brain and mind in some fascinating ways, from increasing your brain function to regulating your emotions. However, the precise effects vary according to whether you engage in short, fast running or long-distance running.","cn":"\"一次60分钟的跑步可以为你的生命增加7小时。\"这是《泰晤士报》上周提出的一项声明。该声明基于一项关于跑步效果的新研究综述。该综述得出结论,跑步者平均比不跑步者多活3年,并且跑步比任何其他形式的运动都更能延长寿命。但跑步的意义不仅仅在于其健康益处。近年来发表的研究表明,跑步以一些引人入胜的方式改变你的大脑和思维,从提高大脑功能到调节情绪。然而,具体效果因你从事短距离快速跑步还是长距离跑步而异。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"For example, in one study, researchers compared participants' ability to learn new words after several minutes of intense running and after 40 minutes of gentle running.","cn":"例如,在一项研究中,研究人员比较了参与者在几分钟高强度跑步后和40分钟温和跑步后学习新单词的能力。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Participants were able to learn 20 percent faster after the intense running and they showed a superior memory when tested again a week later.","cn":"参与者在高强度跑步后学习速度提高了20%,并且在一周后再次测试时表现出更优异的记忆力。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"In another study, researchers asked volunteers to jog for 30 minutes and then showed them clips from a sad movie.","cn":"在另一项研究中,研究人员要求志愿者慢跑30分钟,然后向他们播放悲伤电影的片段。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Participants who usually struggled to handle negative emotions were more intensely affected by the sad clips, just as you'd expect.","cn":"通常难以处理负面情绪的参与者受到悲伤片段的影响更为强烈,正如你所预期的那样。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But crucially, this was less so if they had completed the 30-minute jog.","cn":"但关键的是,如果他们完成了30分钟的慢跑,这种影响会有所减轻。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The researchers said moderate exercise appears to have helped those participants to be less vulnerable to the impact of the sad movie.","cn":"研究人员表示,适度运动似乎帮助这些参与者减少了对悲伤电影影响的脆弱性。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Welcome to the tour of the Hill House.","cn":"欢迎参观Hill House。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"This house built in 1904 is one of the most well-known works of Charles Hill, the famous architect.","cn":"这座建于1904年的房子是著名建筑师Charles Hill最知名的作品之一。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"It was designed and built for a local entrepreneur and his family.","cn":"它是为一位当地企业家及其家人设计和建造的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Before starting the tour, let me give you a brief introduction about the design of this amazing building.","cn":"在开始参观之前,让我简要介绍一下这座令人惊叹的建筑的设计。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Prior to beginning his design, the architect spent some time in the client's old home, observing their life and studying their habits.","cn":"在开始设计之前,建筑师在客户的老房子里待了一段时间,观察他们的生活并研究他们的习惯。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"This meant that he could design the house according to the needs of the family.","cn":"这意味着他可以根据这个家庭的需求来设计房子。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The client's main desire was to have a home with the unique design, so the architect was given complete freedom.","cn":"客户的主要愿望是拥有一座设计独特的房子,因此建筑师获得了完全的自由。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The building style is radically different from what was the fashion of the period.","cn":"这座建筑的风格与当时的流行风格截然不同。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"At the time, most large homes were constructed of timber and brick.","cn":"那时,大多数大型住宅都是用木材和砖块建造的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"This one, however, is made of concrete, a novel construction material in those days.","cn":"然而,这座房子是用混凝土建造的,这在当时是一种新颖的建筑材料。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"The interior of the house, including fittings and furniture, was also designed by the same person.","cn":"房子的内部,包括装置和家具,也是由同一个人设计的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Most of the furniture you will see is original and in good condition.","cn":"你将看到的大部分家具都是原件且保存完好。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"However, those pieces in the children's bedrooms are copies built to the designs of the architect.","cn":"然而,儿童卧室里的那些家具是按照建筑师的设计建造的复制品。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Fortunately, all the blueprints for both the building and its contents have been preserved, so we've been able to replace badly damaged furniture.","cn":"幸运的是,建筑及其内部陈设的所有蓝图都被保存了下来,所以我们能够更换严重损坏的家具。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 3","en":"Let's begin our tour, starting from the rooms.","cn":"让我们开始参观吧,从这些房间开始。"}]},{"id":"cet6-2021-06-2","level":"CET6","exam":"2021_06_2","year":2021,"month":6,"set":2,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2021年6月 六级第2套 · 听力真题","source":"2021年6月 CET-6 第2套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2021/cet6-2021-06-set2.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: How are you enjoying your new job?","cn":"M: 你觉得新工作怎么样？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: So far, so good, I don't miss having managers who deliver blunt, harsh feedback in the name of efficiency.","cn":"W: 到目前为止，一切都不错。我一点也不怀念那些以效率为名，给出直白而严厉反馈的经理。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: From the way you described your last company, no wonder they had a problem with high staff turnover.","cn":"M: 从你描述上一家公司的情况来看，难怪他们会有员工流动率高的问题。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Yeah.","cn":"W: 是啊。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I couldn't wait to get out of there once my contract expired.","cn":"合同一到期，我就迫不及待地离开了那里。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"The problem with a company culture that prizes directness above all else is that it creates a toxic culture of brilliant jerks that drives people out and erodes itself from within.","cn":"一种把直率看得高于一切的公司文化，问题在于它会造就一种充满才华却为人刻薄的有毒文化，把员工赶走，并从内部逐渐瓦解自身。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: My company's managers tend to be accommodating and kind, overlooking mistakes or issues so as not to hurt feelings.","cn":"M: 我们公司的经理往往比较体谅人，也很友善，为了不伤害员工的感情，他们会忽略错误或问题。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Issues often get ignored there until they build up and reach a crisis point.","cn":"那里的问题经常一直被忽视，直到越积越多，最终演变成危机。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: That's not surprising.","cn":"W: 这并不奇怪。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"My new company seems to employ a feedback policy that combines compassion and directness.","cn":"我现在的公司似乎采用了一套兼顾同理心和直率的反馈政策。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Employees have the power to speak up, give feedback, disagree and discuss problems in real time.","cn":"员工有权表达自己的看法、提出反馈、表示不同意见，并实时讨论问题。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It seems to help us to course correct, improve and meet challenges while also building teams that collaborate and care for one another.","cn":"这似乎有助于我们及时调整方向、不断改进、应对挑战，同时也能建立起彼此协作、互相关心的团队。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: But that would be based on an atmosphere of mutual trust, wouldn't it?","cn":"M: 但这应该建立在相互信任的氛围之上，对吧？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Otherwise, people might interpret feedback as some kind of personal attack.","cn":"否则，人们可能会把反馈理解成某种人身攻击。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: True.","cn":"W: 没错。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Without an atmosphere of trust, feedback can create stress and self-doubt.","cn":"没有信任的氛围，反馈可能会带来压力和自我怀疑。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But I think when we get feedback from someone we trust, we understand that the feedback isn't some kind of personal attack.","cn":"但我认为，当我们从信任的人那里得到反馈时，我们会明白这并不是什么人身攻击。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It's actually a kind of support because it's offered in the spirit of helping us improve.","cn":"实际上，这是一种支持，因为对方是本着帮助我们进步的态度提出反馈的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I think sometimes people need to shift their mindsets around how they receive feedback.","cn":"我觉得，有时候人们需要改变自己接受反馈的心态。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Yes.","cn":"M: 是的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Constructive feedback, after all, is how we learn and grow.","cn":"毕竟，建设性的反馈正是我们学习和成长的方式。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"It's the basis for healthy parenting, lasting friendships, career development, and so much more.","cn":"它是健康亲子关系、长久友谊、职业发展的基础，作用远不止这些。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"If we shelter our children, friends, and colleagues from information that might enrich and enhance their lives, we're not being caring.","cn":"如果我们不让孩子、朋友和同事接触那些可能丰富并改善他们生活的信息，那就不是在关心他们。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"We're actually doing harm to them.","cn":"实际上，我们是在伤害他们。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: That's exactly right.","cn":"W: 完全正确。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: How was your holiday?","cn":"W: 你的假期过得怎么样？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Not too many other tourists around, were there?","cn":"周围没太多其他游客吧？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: No, very few relatively.","cn":"M: 没有，相对来说非常少。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"But I found myself moving from one accommodation to another, trying to find the perfect place.","cn":"但我发现自己一直从一个住处搬到另一个住处，试图找到最完美的地方。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It made me realize that indecision is a big problem for me.","cn":"这让我意识到，优柔寡断对我来说是个大问题。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Instead of relaxing, I was looking for the best spot.","cn":"我没有放松下来，反而一直在寻找最好的地方。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: It seems you suffer from \"Fear of Better Options.\" I've read about it. It describes this loop of indecision as part of our programming. Essentially, we have this tendency to keep stretching out the decision-making process, because as human beings, we are hard-wired to optimize. We have always looked to get the best things we can as a sort of survival of the fittest. Optimizing isn't the problem, but rather the process that we go through.","cn":"W: 看来你患有“更好选择恐惧症”。我读过相关的内容。它把这种优柔寡断的循环描述为我们思维机制的一部分。从本质上说，我们总是倾向于不断延长决策过程，因为作为人类，我们天生就会追求最优选择。一直以来，我们都在努力获得能得到的最好东西，这可以说是一种适者生存。追求最优并不是问题，问题在于我们所经历的过程。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Well, that makes me feel better.","cn":"M: 嗯，这让我感觉好受多了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"But I think thanks to technology, we can make comparisons more easily and have more access to choice and customization.","cn":"但我觉得多亏了科技，我们可以更容易地进行比较，也能有更多选择和定制的机会。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"We can now see what we could have, how we might get it, and what others have that we might want.","cn":"现在我们可以看到自己可能拥有什么、可能如何得到它，以及别人拥有而我们可能想要的东西。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"We keep looking over and return to the same options again and again.","cn":"我们不断回头查看，又一次次回到相同的选项上。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Yes.","cn":"W: 是的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"\"Fear of Better Options\" offers little benefit.","cn":"“更好选择恐惧症”几乎没有什么好处。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"It's an ailment of abundance.","cn":"这是过度丰富带来的问题。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"You must have choices to have that fear of missing out on better options.","cn":"你必须拥有选择，才会害怕错过更好的选项。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Yes, I need to note when I'm worrying about inconsequential things, I guess.","cn":"M: 是的，我想我需要留意自己什么时候在为无关紧要的事情操心。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"If I'm spending too much time worrying over what to have for lunch, I'm robbing myself of the energy to focus on the things that matter.","cn":"如果我花太多时间纠结午饭吃什么，就等于消耗了自己的精力，没法专注于真正重要的事情。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Exactly.","cn":"W: 没错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"But for more important matters, I think gut instinct might be overrated.","cn":"不过对于更重要的事情，我觉得凭直觉行事可能被高估了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"When you have 30 odd options, trusting your gut is not practical.","cn":"当你有三十来个选项时，相信直觉并不实际。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"What you need to do is research: have a process, invest time exploring your options, and eliminate as many things as you can.","cn":"你需要做的是进行调查研究：建立一个流程，投入时间去了解各种选择，并尽可能排除更多选项。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"The most toxic part of decision making is going over the same options time and time again.","cn":"决策过程中最有害的部分，就是一遍又一遍地重复考虑相同的选项。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The role of homework in classrooms is not a new debate.","cn":"家庭作业在课堂教学中的作用并不是一个新争论。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Many parents and teachers are ardent supporters of homework.","cn":"许多家长和教师都是家庭作业的热烈支持者。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"But do all students benefit from homework?","cn":"但所有学生都能从家庭作业中受益吗？"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"A 2006 research paper suggested some correlation between the amount of homework done by a student and future academic achievement for middle and high school students but not so much for younger kids.","cn":"2006年的一篇研究论文指出，对于初中和高中生而言，学生完成的作业量与未来的学业成就之间存在一定的相关性，但对于年龄更小的孩子来说则不然。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"A Stanford study in 2014 suggested the same was true for students in California's affluent communities. The findings challenged the idea that homework was \"inherently good.\" The researchers concluded that there was an upper limit to the correlation between homework and achievement, suggesting that high school students shouldn't be doing more than two hours of homework a night. And the most valuable kind of homework for elementary-level children was simply assigned free reading.","cn":"2014年斯坦福大学的一项研究表明，加利福尼亚州富裕社区的学生也是如此。研究结果挑战了家庭作业“本质上是有益的”这一观念。研究人员得出结论，家庭作业与学业成就之间的相关性存在上限，并建议高中生每晚做家庭作业的时间不应超过两小时。而对于小学阶段的孩子来说，最有价值的家庭作业仅仅是布置的自由阅读。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The topic gets more complicated when we talk about the divide between rural and urban communities.","cn":"当我们谈到城乡社区之间的差距时，这个话题变得更加复杂。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Studies found that in remote areas, the poor quality or lack of internet access can put students at a disadvantage because 70% of teachers in these areas assign homework that requires internet access.","cn":"研究发现，在偏远地区，网络质量差或缺乏网络连接会使学生处于不利地位，因为这些地区70%的教师布置的家庭作业都需要使用网络。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"But one in three households doesn't have internet.","cn":"但三分之一的家庭没有网络。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Experts assert homework requiring the internet isn't fair.","cn":"专家断言，需要使用网络的家庭作业是不公平的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"While the debate continues about the effect of homework on academic achievements, there are studies focusing on other benefits of homework.","cn":"尽管关于家庭作业对学业成就影响的争论仍在继续，但也有研究关注家庭作业的其他益处。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"A study in Germany found that homework could have an effect on students' personalities, suggesting that doing homework might help kids to become more conscientious and independent learners.","cn":"德国的一项研究发现，家庭作业可能会对学生的性格产生影响，这表明做家庭作业可能有助于孩子们成为更认真尽责、更独立的学习者。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Robert Goddard, an American born in 1882, is widely regarded as the world's first rocket scientist.","cn":"罗伯特·戈达德是一位1882年出生的美国人，被广泛认为是世界上第一位火箭科学家。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"At age 27, Goddard published his first book in which he hypothesized that a rocket launched from Earth could reach the Moon.","cn":"27岁时，戈达德出版了他的第一本书，在书中提出了从地球发射的火箭可以抵达月球的假说。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Like many visionaries, the young scientist encountered numerous skeptics.","cn":"像许多有远见的人一样，这位年轻的科学家遇到了众多质疑者。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"In January 1920, The New York Times ridiculed Goddard's theory that rockets could be utilized for space exploration.","cn":"1920年1月，《纽约时报》嘲笑了戈达德关于火箭可以用于太空探索的理论。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Forty-nine years later, Apollo 11 reached the Moon and the famed newspaper published an apology to Goddard.","cn":"49年后，阿波罗11号抵达月球，这家著名报纸发表了一篇向戈达德道歉的文章。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Goddard launched his first rocket from an aunt's farm in his native Massachusetts in March, 1926.","cn":"1926年3月，戈达德从家乡马萨诸塞州一位姨母的农场发射了他的第一枚火箭。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"His maiden rocket voyage lasted a mere 3 seconds.","cn":"这枚火箭的首次飞行仅持续了3秒。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It scaled an altitude of only 12 meters.","cn":"它达到的高度只有12米。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Nonetheless, it was a milestone in rocket science.","cn":"尽管如此，这仍是火箭科学领域的一个里程碑。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Goddard later consulted with a weather expert and determined that the climate of New Mexico was ideal for year-round rocket launches.","cn":"后来，戈达德向一位气象专家进行了咨询，并确定新墨西哥州的气候非常适合全年发射火箭。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"In 1930, Goddard and his family relocated there, to a remote valley in the southwest of the country.","cn":"1930年，戈达德和家人搬到了那里，定居在美国西南部一个偏远的山谷中。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"There he established a laboratory and test range.","cn":"他在那里建立了一个实验室和试验场。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"However, the ambitious scientist received negligible support from the government.","cn":"然而，这位雄心勃勃的科学家几乎没有得到政府的支持。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"For four years, wealthy businessman Daniel Guggenheim provided Goddard with an annual 25,000 dollars grant to pursue his dreams.","cn":"四年来，富有的商人丹尼尔·古根海姆每年向戈达德提供2.5万美元的资助，以支持他追逐梦想。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Other rocket enthusiasts also raised funds for him.","cn":"其他火箭爱好者也为他筹集资金。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Over time, Goddard's rocket grew more sophisticated and included the installation of instruments.","cn":"随着时间的推移，戈达德的火箭变得越来越复杂，并增设了各种仪器。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"In spite of his many successes, Goddard was never able to interest the US military in rocket-propelled weapons.","cn":"尽管取得了许多成功，戈达德始终未能使美国军方对火箭推进武器产生兴趣。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"He was granted over 200 patents and continued to pioneer rocket technology until his death in 1945.","cn":"他获得了200多项专利，并一直致力于开创火箭技术，直到1945年去世。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Working for a new venture comes with a lot of risks.","cn":"为一家新创企业工作伴随着诸多风险。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"There's instability, unclear responsibilities, and the need to be a master of all trades.","cn":"企业可能缺乏稳定性，职责也不明确，而且需要一个人样样都能胜任。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"But the primary benefit is usually the passion and excitement associated with playing a role in a promising new company.","cn":"但其主要益处通常在于，能够参与一家前景可观的新公司，并从中获得激情与兴奋感。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The person to thank for that passion and excitement is almost always the entrepreneur.","cn":"几乎总是应该感谢企业家的，正是这种激情与兴奋感。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"There's something about the founder's energy and enthusiasm that infects the rest of the team.","cn":"创始人的活力与热情总有一种感染团队其他成员的力量。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The willingness to take risks may inspire others to be more courageous.","cn":"敢于承担风险的意愿可能会激励他人变得更加勇敢。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The optimism and positivity may motivate people to focus less on trivial and unimportant matters.","cn":"乐观积极的态度可能促使人们少关注琐碎且无关紧要的事情。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The celebration of milestones may prompt staff to be more grateful about their own accomplishments and privileges.","cn":"对里程碑的庆祝可能会促使员工更加感激自己的成就与所拥有的优势。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"What becomes set in the firm's culture is a contagious collection of affirmative and positive emotions which are usually shared among the team. Science has already done a good job of proving the results that follow. These include better processes, greater team cohesion, reduced conflict and sharper alertness.","cn":"最终融入公司文化的，是一系列具有传染性的肯定且积极的情绪，而这些情绪通常会在团队成员之间共享。科学研究已经很好地证明了随之而来的结果，其中包括更完善的流程、更强的团队凝聚力、更少的冲突以及更加敏锐的警觉性。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"But what is yet to be demonstrated is whether the founder's passion leads to increased team performance.","cn":"但创始人的激情是否会带来团队绩效的提升，尚未得到证明。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"This was recently tested in research, which analyzed the teams of 73 new companies across a range of industries such as IT, medicine and energy.","cn":"最近，一项研究对此进行了检验，分析了73家新公司的团队，这些公司涵盖IT、医疗和能源等多个行业。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The CEOs were consulted once again, years after the initial analysis.","cn":"研究人员在初次分析数年后再次向这些公司的首席执行官进行了咨询。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"And most shared their firm's performance reports, so that their success could be more objectively measured.","cn":"大多数首席执行官都提供了公司的绩效报告，从而使研究人员能够更加客观地衡量其成功程度。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Entrepreneurial teams generally progress through three phases.","cn":"创业团队通常会经历三个阶段。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The first is inventing a product or service, the second is founding the venture to sell that product or service, and the third is developing the firm so it continues to grow.","cn":"第一阶段是发明一种产品或服务，第二阶段是创办企业来销售该产品或服务，第三阶段则是发展公司，使其能够持续增长。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The researchers discovered that when the team is passionate about the third phase—developing the firm—there's a clear link to performance.","cn":"研究人员发现，当团队对第三阶段，也就是发展公司，充满热情时，这与绩效之间存在明确的联系。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"But the first phase—a passion for invention—is not a reliable indicator that the firm will still be open for business a few years later.","cn":"但第一阶段，即对发明的热情，并不能可靠地表明这家公司几年后仍会继续营业。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Likewise, the second—a passion for founding the venture—doesn't necessarily translate into great success.","cn":"同样，第二阶段，即对创办企业的热情，也未必能转化为巨大的成功。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The solution to great team performance stems from a willingness to recruit others who could direct their passion towards the third phase of entrepreneurialism: developing the business.","cn":"团队取得出色绩效的关键，在于愿意招募那些能够将热情投入创业第三阶段，即发展业务的人。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Employing more staff can in itself be a risk for an entrepreneur, as is paying them big dollars to attract them.","cn":"雇用更多员工本身就可能给企业家带来风险，为了吸引他们而支付高额薪酬也是如此。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"On many occasions, the entrepreneurs reported not paying themselves a wage at all initially, in order to cover salaries and expenses.","cn":"在许多情况下，企业家都表示，起初为了支付员工薪资和各项开支，他们甚至完全不给自己发工资。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Ageing is a curious thing and people's desire to beat it—and death—has become an industry worth hundreds of billions of dollars.","cn":"衰老是一件奇妙的事情，而人们想要战胜衰老乃至死亡的愿望，已经催生了一个价值数千亿美元的产业。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Despite the huge investment into research, ageing remains somewhat obscure, although there are certain things researchers do understand.","cn":"尽管投入了巨资进行研究，衰老仍然在一定程度上鲜为人知，不过研究人员确实了解一些情况。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"They know that women tend to have longer lifespans, living on average six years longer than men.","cn":"他们知道，女性往往寿命更长，平均比男性多活六年。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"No one is really certain of the reason for this, although the speculation centers around the idea that women are more capable of surviving or handling disease than men.","cn":"没有人真正确定其中的原因，不过有人推测，这可能是因为女性比男性更有能力挺过疾病或应对疾病。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"For virtually every disease, the effects are greater on men than they are on women.","cn":"几乎对于每一种疾病，男性受到的影响都比女性更大。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Some suggest that women's immune systems benefit from their tendency to prioritize and nurture social connections.","cn":"有人认为，女性倾向于优先维系和培养社会关系，这使她们的免疫系统受益。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But for me, this explanation is hardly convincing.","cn":"但对我而言，这种解释很难令人信服。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Researchers also know, to an extent, what causes ageing.","cn":"研究人员也在一定程度上了解衰老的原因。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"For 60 years, it was believed that cells would continue to divide forever.","cn":"在长达60年的时间里，人们一直认为细胞会不断分裂下去，永远不会停止。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"It was only uncovered in relatively recent times that older people's cells divide a smaller number of times than younger people's.","cn":"直到相对较近的时期，人们才发现，老年人的细胞分裂次数少于年轻人的。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Only cancer cells, in fact, are capable of dividing forever.","cn":"事实上，只有癌细胞能够无限分裂。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Human cells have a limited reproductive ability.","cn":"人体细胞的繁殖能力是有限的。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"To an extent, we can postpone the eventual stop of cells' dividing, through nutrition, exercise, good sleep, and even relaxation techniques.","cn":"在一定程度上，我们可以通过营养、锻炼、良好的睡眠，甚至放松技巧，推迟细胞最终停止分裂的时间。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But we cannot stop the ageing process.","cn":"但我们无法阻止衰老过程。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"And researchers are yet to answer the ultimate question of ageing. Why does the body ultimately fall to pieces?","cn":"而研究人员尚未回答有关衰老的终极问题：身体最终为什么会衰败？"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In the opinion of some of the world's best scientific minds on the subject, part of the reason we don't yet have an answer is because many researchers are looking in the wrong direction.","cn":"在该领域一些世界顶尖科学家的看法中，我们至今尚未找到答案，部分原因在于许多研究人员的研究方向错了。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Many public health policy makers believe that the resolution of age-associated disease will tell us something fundamental about the ageing process, but say some top scientists, that's completely erroneous.","cn":"许多公共卫生政策制定者认为，解决与年龄相关的疾病将使我们了解衰老过程中的某些根本问题，但一些顶尖科学家说，这种看法完全错误。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"They point to when the diseases of childhood were eliminated, but this did not provide any insight into childhood development.","cn":"他们指出，儿童期疾病被消除之后，并没有因此让人们对儿童成长发育有任何深入了解。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In the same way, the idea that the resolution of age-associated disease like heart disease and stroke will inform us about ageing is not based on sound science or logic.","cn":"同样，认为解决心脏病和中风等与年龄相关的疾病就能让我们了解衰老，这一想法没有坚实的科学或逻辑依据。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"At best, if the major causes of death in developed countries were eliminated, this would only add a decade to average life expectancy.","cn":"充其量，即使发达国家消除了导致死亡的主要原因，也只能使平均预期寿命增加十年。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But while there is money available to be spent on it, the search to understand the secrets of ageing will be ongoing.","cn":"不过，只要还有资金可以投入，对衰老奥秘的探索就将持续下去。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Good afternoon.","cn":"下午好。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"In today's talk, we'll discuss how managers can get their staff to do what they are asked.","cn":"今天的讲座中，我们将讨论管理者如何让员工按照要求完成工作。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Much to their frustration, managers often struggle to get their staff to comply with even simple instructions.","cn":"令管理者深感沮丧的是，他们常常难以让员工遵守哪怕是简单的指示。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Often they blame their employees: \"They don't read emails, they don't listen, they don't care\"-that kind of thing.","cn":"他们往往把责任归咎于员工：“他们不读邮件，不听指示，也不在乎——诸如此类。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But according to recent research conducted in Australia, it looks like it's not the employees' fault but the managers'.","cn":"”但根据澳大利亚近期开展的一项研究，问题似乎不在员工，而在管理者。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It's easy to understand why people sometimes disobey procedures intentionally.","cn":"人们有时会故意不遵守程序，这一点很容易理解。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Occasionally, it's because they're pressured to finish in a short time.","cn":"有时是因为他们受到压力，必须在很短的时间内完成工作。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"At other times, they may disagree with the spirit of the procedure, the effort demanded, the time consumed, the lack of potential effectiveness.","cn":"另一些时候，他们可能不同意程序的宗旨，或认为程序要求付出的努力太多、耗费的时间太长，或者潜在的成效不足。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"And every now and then, they just don't want to, maybe deliberately or out of stubbornness.","cn":"还有些时候，他们只是不想遵守，可能是故意如此，也可能是出于固执。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"So apart from that, what else gets in the way of procedural compliance?","cn":"那么，除此之外，还有什么因素会妨碍人们遵守程序呢？"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The research scholars surveyed 152 blue-collar workers from two separate sites in the mining industry.","cn":"研究人员对采矿业两个不同工作地点的152名蓝领工人进行了调查。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"They asked the workers a range of procedure-related questions, such as whether they found the procedures useful, how confident they felt in their job, how comfortable they were to speak up in the workplace, and how closely they followed any new procedures set by their managers.","cn":"他们向工人提出了一系列与程序有关的问题，例如他们是否认为这些程序有用、对自己的工作有多大信心、在工作场所发言时是否感到自在，以及他们在多大程度上遵循管理者制定的任何新程序。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"They were also asked to rate the extent to which they perceived their supervisors to be helpful.","cn":"他们还被要求评价自己认为主管在多大程度上能够提供帮助。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"That last statement was the most instructive because, as the researchers found, there was a remarkably strong correlation between how helpful supervisors were perceived to be and how likely their employees were to follow their directives.","cn":"最后一点最能说明问题，因为研究人员发现，人们认为主管是否乐于提供帮助，与员工是否愿意遵循主管的指示之间存在显著的强相关性。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Supervisors' helping behavior was found to be motivational in nature.","cn":"研究发现，主管的帮助行为具有激励作用。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It increased employees' perception of the likelihood of success in the attainment of job goals, and therefore fostered a willingness to dedicate their effort and ability to their work.","cn":"这种行为提高了员工对实现工作目标成功可能性的认识，因此促使他们愿意将自己的努力和能力投入工作。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"In short, managers should be ongoing role models for the change.","cn":"简而言之，管理者应当持续以身作则，推动变革。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"As the saying goes: \"Do as I do, not as I say\".","cn":"正如俗话所说：“照我做，而不是照我说的做。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"To affect behavioral change, what's most required is interaction and involvement—the human touch—and, naturally, processes that add value.","cn":"”要促进行为改变，最需要的是互动和参与——人与人之间的沟通——当然还需要能够创造价值的流程。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Although procedures are designed to guide and support employees' work, employees, it seems, can't always be expected to comply with procedures that are not seen as useful.","cn":"虽然程序旨在指导和支持员工的工作，但看来，我们不能总是期待员工遵守那些被认为没有用处的程序。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"And of course, managers shouldn't keep resending emails.","cn":"当然，管理者也不应一遍遍地重新发送邮件。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"They're an effective tool for the sharing of data and reports, but they're a hopeless tool if what a manager is desiring is a change in behavior.","cn":"邮件是分享数据和报告的有效工具，但如果管理者想要改变员工的行为，邮件就完全不起作用了。"}]},{"id":"cet6-2021-12-1","level":"CET6","exam":"2021_12_1","year":2021,"month":12,"set":1,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2021年12月 六级第1套 · 听力真题","source":"2021年12月 CET-6 第1套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2021/cet6-2021-12-set1.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Hi, David.","cn":"W: 嗨，戴维。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I haven't seen you in class for almost two weeks.","cn":"我快两周没在课堂上见到你了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"We thought you had disappeared on holiday early or something.","cn":"我们还以为你提早休假去哪里了呢。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Hi, Sarah.","cn":"M: 嗨，莎拉。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Well, it's a bit of a long story I'm afraid.","cn":"唉，说来话长。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I got a throat infection last week and had to go to the hospital to get some antibiotics as I really wasn't getting any better.","cn":"我上周喉咙感染了，因为病情实在不见好转，不得不去医院开了一些抗生素。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Oh yeah.","cn":"W: 哦，是的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"There have been so many viruses going around this winter.","cn":"今年冬天有好多病毒在传播。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"The weather has been so awful for the last few weeks.","cn":"过去几周的天气真是太糟了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: And, on the way back from the hospital, I slipped on some ice and fell and then had to go to the hospital to get an X-ray because I basically thought I broke my wrist, although, thankfully, it's not broken.","cn":"M: 还有，在从医院回来的路上，我在冰上滑倒摔了一跤，结果又得去医院拍 X 光，因为我以为自己把手腕给摔断了，不过幸好没断。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But I need to be careful with it for the next few weeks.","cn":"但接下来的几周我得小心对待这只手。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Oh, that's too bad!","cn":"W: 哦，那太糟糕了！"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"How unfortunate!","cn":"真是太倒霉了！"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: To make things worse, I managed to fall right in front of four girls from the ninth grade.","cn":"M: 更糟糕的是，我偏偏摔在了四个九年级女生面前。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"So I was utterly humiliated.","cn":"简直丢脸丢到家了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Plus, the laptop in my bag was broken too.","cn":"而且，我包里的笔记本电脑也摔坏了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: No, what a complete catastrophe!","cn":"W: 天啊，这真是彻头彻尾的灾难！"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Is the laptop still under warranty?","cn":"笔记本电脑还在保修期内吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"If it is, then you can easily send it back to the manufacturer, and they'll send you a brand-new one for free surely.","cn":"如果是的话，你就可以很方便地寄回给厂家，他们肯定会免费给你寄一台全新的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: The warranty ran out three days before I broke it.","cn":"M: 保修期在我摔坏它的前三天就过了。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"And all my essays are in there, and I need to hand them in before we break for the Christmas holidays.","cn":"我所有的论文都在里面，而且我必须在放圣诞假之前把它们交上去。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Listen, I have the number of a really good, affordable computer repair shop at home.","cn":"W: 听我说，我家里有一家又好又实惠的电脑维修店的电话。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"My dad has used this guy before and he can work miracles.","cn":"我爸爸以前找过这个人，他简直能创造奇迹。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Let's go back to my house and we can call the repair shop, and you can have some tea and cookies too.","cn":"我们回我家吧，我们可以给维修店打电话，你还可以喝点茶、吃点饼干。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Wow, thanks, Sarah!","cn":"M: 哇，谢谢你，莎拉！"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"That would be great!","cn":"那太好了！"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Let me just call my mom and let her know I'll be home a little bit later.","cn":"我先给我妈妈打个电话，跟她说一声我会晚一点回家。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Welcome to this week's episode of Book Talk.","cn":"M: 欢迎收听本周的《图书谈》。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"With me today is Heidi Brown, a historian who has written five critically acclaimed books about military history.","cn":"今天和我一起做节目的是海蒂·布朗，她是一位历史学家，已经写了五本广受评论界好评的军事史著作。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Thanks for having me, John.","cn":"W: 谢谢你邀请我，约翰。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I'm so excited to talk about my latest book, which was published last month.","cn":"我非常高兴能聊聊我的最新著作，这本书上个月刚刚出版。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: So this book is a novel, your first attempt at that genre.","cn":"M: 所以，这本书是一部小说，是你第一次尝试这一体裁。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I thought it was a bit of a departure for you.","cn":"我觉得这对你来说是一个不小的转变。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I'd say it's a major departure as it's not just a work of fiction. It's set 200 years in the future.","cn":"W: 我会说这是一次很大的转变，因为它不只是一部虚构作品，故事还设定在两百年后的未来。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Right.","cn":"M: 好。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So how did that happen?","cn":"那么这是怎么发生的？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"You spent three decades writing about the past and focusing on the 18th and 19th centuries.","cn":"你花了三十年时间写过去的历史，重点关注十八世纪和十九世纪。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And now you're speculating about the future.","cn":"现在却开始推测未来。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Well, after years of researching soldiers and chronicling their lives during battle, I just started wondering about other facets of their lives, especially their personal lives.","cn":"W: 嗯，多年来研究士兵并记录他们在战斗中的生活之后，我开始思考他们生活中的其他方面，尤其是他们的私人生活。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: I can see that.","cn":"M: 我能理解。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Your novel is about soldiers and it focuses on their relationships, especially the bond between sons and mothers and men and their wives.","cn":"你的小说写的是士兵，重点讲述他们之间的关系，尤其是儿子与母亲之间的感情，以及男人与妻子之间的联系。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Yes.","cn":"W: 是的。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"That focus came about when I still intended to write another book of history.","cn":"我最初打算再写一本历史书时，就产生了这个关注点。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"I started by researching soldiers' actual personal lives, studying their letters home.","cn":"我先研究士兵真实的私人生活，研读他们寄回家的信件。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: So how did that history book become a novel?","cn":"M: 那么，这本历史书后来是怎么变成小说的？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Well, I realized that the historical record was incomplete.","cn":"W: 嗯，我意识到历史记录并不完整。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So I'd either have to leave a lot of gaps or make a lot more assumptions than a historian should.","cn":"所以，我要么得留下许多空白，要么就得做出远超历史学家应有程度的大量推断。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: But why write a novel set in the future when your credentials are perfect for a historical novel?","cn":"M: 但既然你的资历非常适合写历史小说，为什么要写一部以未来为背景的小说呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"As a historian, any historical novel you write would have a lot of credibility.","cn":"作为一名历史学家，无论你写什么历史小说，都会很有可信度。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: I felt too constrained working with the past, like what I wrote needed to be fact as opposed to fiction, but writing about the future gave me more freedom to imagine, to invent.","cn":"W: 我觉得创作过去的题材束缚太多了，好像我写的东西必须是事实，而不能是虚构。但写未来让我有更多自由去想象和创造。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Well, having read your book, I'm glad you made that choice to move into fiction.","cn":"M: 读过你的书之后，我很高兴你做出了转向小说创作的选择。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Whether it's in the hands of animated polar bears or Santa Claus, there's one thing you'll find in nearly all ads for Coca-Cola: the characteristic glass bottle.","cn":"无论是由动画片中的北极熊还是圣诞老人拿着，在几乎所有可口可乐的广告中，你都会看到同一样东西：那只独具特色的玻璃瓶。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Most Americans don't drink soda out of the glass bottles seen in Coke's ads anymore.","cn":"如今，大多数美国人已经不再用可口可乐广告中出现的玻璃瓶喝汽水了。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"But this week, the company is celebrating a century of the bottle that's been sold in more than 200 countries.","cn":"但本周，这家公司正在庆祝这种已在全球200多个国家销售的瓶子问世一百周年。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Flash back to 1915, when a bottle of Coca-Cola cost just a nickel.","cn":"回到1915年，那时一瓶可口可乐只要5美分。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"As the soft drink gained in popularity, it faced a growing number of competitors—counterfeits even trying to copy Coke's logo.","cn":"随着这种软饮料越来越受欢迎，它面临的竞争者也越来越多，甚至还有仿冒品试图复制可口可乐的标志。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"So, according to Coca-Cola historian Ted Ryan, the company decided to come up with packaging that couldn't be duplicated.","cn":"因此，据可口可乐历史学家特德·瑞安介绍，公司决定设计一种无法仿制的包装。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"A product request was sent to eight different glass makers.","cn":"公司向八家不同的玻璃制造商发出了一份产品设计要求。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Workers at the Root Glass Company got the request and began flipping through the encyclopedia at the local library, landing on cocoa seed.","cn":"鲁特玻璃公司的工人收到要求后，开始在当地的图书馆翻阅百科全书，最后注意到了可可种子。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Though cocoa seed is not an ingredient of the soda, they designed their bottle based on the seed's shape and large middle.","cn":"虽然可可种子并不是这种汽水的原料，但他们根据种子的形状和中部较大的特点设计了瓶子。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"It won over Coke executives in Atlanta and would go on to receive its own trademark, spur collections and earn Coca-Cola an iconic image that made it part of American culture for a century.","cn":"这一设计赢得了亚特兰大可口可乐公司高管的认可，后来还获得了自己的商标，推动了收藏热潮，并为可口可乐赢得了一个具有标志性的形象，使其在一个世纪里成为美国文化的一部分。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"It was 100 years ago this week that the bottle earned a patent.","cn":"就在本周之前的一百年前，这种瓶子获得了专利。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"By World War II, Coke bottle sales had ballooned into billions.","cn":"到第二次世界大战时，可口可乐瓶装产品的销量已经达到数十亿瓶。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Americans mostly consume Coke out of aluminum or plastic today, but the glass bottle remains a symbol of America that's readily recognized around the world.","cn":"如今，美国人饮用可口可乐时主要使用铝罐或塑料瓶，但这种玻璃瓶仍然是美国的象征，在世界各地都很容易被认出。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Research shows that a few moments of conversation with a stranger creates a measurable improvement in mood.","cn":"研究表明，与陌生人进行短暂的交谈能使情绪得到明显的改善。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But most of us are reluctant to start these conversations because we presume the opposite.","cn":"但我们大多数人都不愿意开启这些对话，因为我们以为情况恰恰相反。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"In an experiment, commuters who talked to nearby strangers found their commute more enjoyable than those who didn't.","cn":"在一项实验中，与身边的陌生人交谈的通勤者发现，他们的通勤过程比那些没有交谈的人更令人愉快。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"They were asked to predict whether they'd enjoy the commute more if they conversed with other people.","cn":"他们被要求预测如果与他人交谈，自己是否会更享受通勤。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Intriguingly, most expected the more solitary experience to be more pleasurable.","cn":"有趣的是，大多数人预想独处的体验会更令人愉快。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Why is this?","cn":"为什么会这样？"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Social anxiety appears to be the problem.","cn":"社交焦虑似乎是问题所在。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"People's reluctance to start conversations with nearby strangers comes partly from \"underestimating others' interest in connecting\".","cn":"人们不愿意与身边的陌生人开启对话，部分原因在于“低估了他人建立联系的兴趣”。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The sad thing is that people presume that a nearby stranger doesn't want to converse and don't start a conversation.","cn":"令人遗憾的是，人们假定身边的陌生人不想交谈，因而没有开启对话。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Only those who forced themselves to chat because it was required by the experiment found out what a pleasant experience it could be.","cn":"只有那些因实验要求而强迫自己聊天的人，才发现这会是多么令人愉快的体验。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Human beings are social animals.","cn":"人类是社交动物。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Those who misunderstand the impact of social interactions may not, in some contexts, be social enough for their own well-being.","cn":"那些误解社交互动影响的人，在某些情况下可能为了自身的幸福感而表现得不够合群。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"You should be chatting with the strangers you encounter.","cn":"你应该与遇到的陌生人聊天。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"You may occasionally have a negative encounter that might stick in your memory.","cn":"你偶尔可能会遇到不愉快的经历，并且可能会留在记忆中。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"This is because the human brain is biased to dwell on negative events.","cn":"这是因为人类大脑倾向于关注负面事件。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"But starting conversations with strangers is still well worth the risk of rejection.","cn":"但冒着被拒绝的风险与陌生人开启对话依然非常值得。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"It may surprise you that conversing with strangers will make them happier too.","cn":"与陌生人交谈也会让他们感到更高兴，这可能会让你感到惊讶。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"The pleasure of connection seems contagious.","cn":"建立联系的乐趣似乎具有传染性。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"People who are talked to have equally positive experiences as those who initiate a conversation.","cn":"被搭话的人与发起对话的人拥有同样积极的体验。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The Caribbean islands are divided into two worlds, a rich one and a poor one.","cn":"加勒比海诸岛被分为两个世界：一个富裕的世界和一个贫困的世界。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"This tropical region's economy is based mainly on farming.","cn":"这个热带地区的经济主要以农业为基础。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Farmers are of two types.","cn":"农民有两种类型。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"One is the plantation owner who may have hundreds of thousands of acres.","cn":"一种是拥有数十万英亩土地的种植园主。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"In contrast, the small cultivator is working only a few acres of land.","cn":"相比之下，小农只耕种几英亩土地。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Most visitors to the Caribbean are rich, like the plantation owner.","cn":"大多数到加勒比海旅游的游客都很富有，就像种植园主一样。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"They do not realize or do not want to realize that many farm families barely managed to get by on what they grow.","cn":"他们没有意识到，或者不愿意识到，许多农民家庭仅靠自己种植的东西勉强维持生计。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The Caribbean produces many things.","cn":"加勒比海地区生产许多东西。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Sugar is the main product.","cn":"糖是主要产品。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Other export crops are tobacco, coffee, bananas, spices and citrus fruits, such as orange, lemon or grapefruit.","cn":"其他出口作物包括烟草、咖啡、香蕉、香料和柑橘类水果，如橙子、柠檬或葡萄柚。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"From the West Indies also come oil, mineral pitch and many forest products.","cn":"西印度群岛还出产石油、矿物沥青和许多林产品。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Jamaica's aluminum ore supplies are the world's largest.","cn":"牙买加的铝矿储量居世界首位。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Oil comes from Trinidad, Aruba and Curacao.","cn":"石油产自特立尼达、阿鲁巴和库拉索。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"But for many of the smaller islands, sugar is the only export.","cn":"但对许多较小的岛屿来说，糖是唯一的出口产品。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Rum, a strong alcoholic drink, which is distilled from sugar cane, is also an export.","cn":"朗姆酒是一种从甘蔗中蒸馏出来的烈性酒，也是一种出口产品。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The world's best rum comes from this area.","cn":"世界上最好的朗姆酒产自这一地区。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Local kinds vary from the light rums of Puerto Rico to the heavier darker rums of Barbados and Jamaica.","cn":"当地朗姆酒的种类各不相同，从波多黎各的淡色朗姆酒，到巴巴多斯和牙买加较为浓烈、颜色较深的朗姆酒都有。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"American tourists enjoy stocking up on inexpensive high quality Caribbean rum while they're on vacation.","cn":"美国游客在度假期间喜欢购买价格低廉而品质优良的加勒比朗姆酒。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"In Curacao, the well-known liquor of that name is made from the thick outer skin of a native orange.","cn":"在库拉索，以该地闻名的酒名命名的利口酒，是用当地一种橙子的厚外皮制成的。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Ever since America's colonial days, the Caribbean islands have been favorite places to visit.","cn":"自美国殖民时期以来，加勒比海诸岛一直是人们喜爱的旅游地。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Since World War II, tourism has increased rapidly.","cn":"第二次世界大战以来，旅游业迅速发展。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Because great numbers of people go there, the islanders have built elaborate resorts, developed harbors and airfields, improved the beaches and have expanded sea and air routes.","cn":"由于前往那里的人数众多，岛民修建了精致的度假胜地，开发了港口和机场，改善了海滩，并扩展了海上和空中航线。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Everything is at the resort-hotel, beach, shopping and recreation.","cn":"度假酒店、海滩、购物和娱乐一应俱全。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The vacationer never has any reason to explore the island.","cn":"度假者完全没有理由去探索这座岛屿。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"As in most places, those who have money live well indeed.","cn":"和大多数地方一样，有钱人确实过着优裕的生活。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Those who don't have money live at various levels of poverty.","cn":"没有钱的人则处于不同程度的贫困之中。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"But here the poor greatly outnumber the wealthy.","cn":"但在这里，穷人的数量远远超过富人。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"A visitor will find rich people living in apartments or Spanish houses at the seaside or in the countryside.","cn":"游客会看到富人住在海边或乡间的公寓里，或者住在西班牙式房屋中。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Their servants might include a cook, a maid, and a nurse for their children.","cn":"他们的仆人可能包括厨师、女佣和照顾孩子的护士。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Most of the people live well below the poverty level.","cn":"大多数人的生活水平远低于贫困线。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"In towns, they live crowded together in tiny houses.","cn":"在城镇里，他们拥挤地住在狭小的房屋中。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Islanders make the best they can of what they have.","cn":"岛民们尽可能利用自己所拥有的一切。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Their homes are quite shabby.","cn":"他们的住房相当破旧。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Sadly, most tourists never see the side of the Caribbean.","cn":"令人遗憾的是，大多数游客从未见过加勒比海的这一面。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Talk to anyone who is a generation or two older, and they would most likely comment that children are more spoiled these days.","cn":"和比自己年长一两代的人交谈，他们很可能会说，如今的孩子更加娇生惯养了。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"No one wants to have or be around demanding, selfish and spoiled children, those who get bad-tempered or silently brood when they are not given everything they want immediately.","cn":"没有人愿意拥有或和那些要求过多、自私且被宠坏的孩子相处；当他们不能立即得到自己想要的一切时，就会变得脾气暴躁或闷闷不乐。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Paradoxically, the parents of such children encourage this demanding behavior in the mistaken belief that by giving their children everything they can their children will be happy.","cn":"矛盾的是，这类孩子的父母却错误地认为，只要尽可能满足孩子的一切要求，孩子就会感到幸福，于是反而助长了这种索取无度的行为。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In the short term, perhaps they are right.","cn":"短期来看，他们或许是对的。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"But in the longer term, such children end up lonely, dependent, chronically dissatisfied and resentful of the parents who tried so hard to please them.","cn":"但从长远来看，这些孩子最终会变得孤独、依赖他人、长期不满，并对那些竭力取悦他们的父母心怀怨恨。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Undoubtedly parents want to raise happy children who are confident, capable and likable rather than spoiled and miserable.","cn":"毫无疑问，父母都希望把孩子培养成幸福、自信、有能力且讨人喜欢的人，而不是被宠坏又不快乐的人。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"One factor hindering this is that parents can't or don't spend enough quality time with their kids, and substitute this deficit with toys, games, gadgets and the like.","cn":"阻碍这一目标的一个因素是，父母无法或没有花足够的高质量时间陪伴孩子，于是用玩具、游戏、电子设备之类的东西来弥补这一不足。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Rather than getting material things, children need parents' devoted attention.","cn":"孩子需要的不是物质上的东西，而是父母全心全意的关注。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The quantity of time spent together is less important than the content of that time.","cn":"共同相处的时间长短并不如相处时光的内容重要。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Instead of instantly satisfying their wishes, parents should help them work out a plan to earn things they'd like to have.","cn":"父母不应立即满足孩子的愿望，而应帮助他们制定计划，通过努力获得自己想要的东西。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"This teaches them to value the effort as well as what it achieves.","cn":"这能教会他们既重视努力本身，也重视努力所取得的成果。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Allow them to enjoy anticipation.","cn":"让孩子享受期待的过程。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Numerous psychological studies have demonstrated that children who learn to wait for things they desire are more likely to succeed in a number of ways later in life.","cn":"大量心理学研究表明，学会等待自己渴望的事物的孩子，日后更有可能在许多方面取得成功。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"One famous experiment in the 1960s involved 3- to 6-year-old children.","cn":"20世纪60年代进行的一项著名实验以3至6岁的儿童为对象。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"They were given a choice between receiving a small reward, such as a cookie, immediately, or if they waited 15 minutes, they could have two.","cn":"他们可以选择立即得到一份小奖励，例如一块饼干；也可以等待15分钟，这样就能得到两块。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Follow up studies have found that those who chose to delay satisfaction are now more academically successful, have greater self-worth, and even tend to be healthier.","cn":"后续研究发现，那些选择延迟满足的孩子，如今在学业上更加成功，自我价值感更强，而且往往也更加健康。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"If they fail, children should be encouraged to keep trying rather than to give up if they really want the desired result.","cn":"如果失败了，只要孩子确实想要达到预期的结果，就应鼓励他们继续尝试，而不是放弃。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"This teaches them how to handle and recover from disappointment, which is associated with greater success and satisfaction academically, financially and in personal relationships.","cn":"这能教会他们如何应对失望并从中恢复，而这与他们在学业、经济状况和个人关系方面取得更大的成功与满足感有关。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"And lastly, parents should encourage their children to look at life from other points of view, as well as their own.","cn":"最后，父母还应鼓励孩子从其他人的角度以及自己的角度看待生活。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"This teaches them to be understanding of and sympathetic towards others—qualities sure to take them a long way in life.","cn":"这能教会他们理解和同情他人，而这些品质必将让他们在人生道路上受益匪浅。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It is not hard to mess up an interview.","cn":"面试出错并不难。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Most people feel nervous sitting across from a hiring manager, answering questions that effectively open themselves up for judgment.","cn":"大多数人坐在招聘经理对面，回答那些实际上会让自己暴露在评判之下的问题时，都会感到紧张。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"And your chances of being more carefully considered for the job can quickly go downhill just by saying the wrong thing at the wrong time.","cn":"仅仅因为在错误的时间说了错误的话，你被更认真地考虑录用的机会就可能迅速下降。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The most obvious thing not to do is complain.","cn":"最明显应该避免的事情就是抱怨。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Employers want to hire positive people.","cn":"雇主希望招聘积极乐观的人。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Talking about a previous job negatively raises concerns that you might be difficult to manage, or you might be someone that blames management for your own poor performance.","cn":"负面谈论上一份工作会引发担忧，让人觉得你可能难以管理，或者你可能是那种把自己的糟糕表现归咎于管理层的人。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Don't say that you've moved around in jobs because you haven't found the right fit or feel that you were not challenged enough.","cn":"不要说你换过多份工作是因为一直没有找到合适的岗位，或者觉得自己没有得到足够的挑战。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Statements like these will make you sound aimless and lost.","cn":"这样的说法会让你听起来漫无目的、迷失方向。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"An interviewer may well think, why would this role be any different for you?","cn":"面试官很可能会想：这个职位对你来说又会有什么不同呢？"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"You will probably leave here in six months.","cn":"你大概六个月后就会离开这里。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It also begs the question of what type of relationship you had with your manager.","cn":"这也会让人不禁思考你和经理之间的关系如何。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It doesn't sound like you had open communication with him or her.","cn":"听起来，你似乎没有与他或她进行坦诚的沟通。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Managers usually love people who can self-sustain and enable growth through taking initiative, who are strong at following through their work, and who bring ideas and solutions to the table.","cn":"经理通常很喜欢那些能够自我驱动、通过主动采取行动促进成长、善于把工作贯彻到底，并且能够提出想法和解决方案的人。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"If you were in a management or leadership position, when discussing your current role, never take all the credit for accomplishments or achievements.","cn":"如果你曾担任管理或领导职位，在谈论当前职位时，绝不要把所有功劳或成就都归于自己。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Emphasize your team and how through their talents, your vision was realized.","cn":"要突出你的团队，以及你是如何凭借他们的才能实现自己的愿景的。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Most successful leaders know that they are only as good as their team.","cn":"大多数成功的领导者都知道，自己的能力取决于团队的表现。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"And acknowledging this in an interview will go a long way towards suggesting that you might be the right person for the position you are applying for.","cn":"在面试中承认这一点，将大大有助于表明你可能正是所申请职位的合适人选。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Lastly, have a good idea of what your role will be and try and convey the idea that you're flexible.","cn":"最后，要清楚了解自己的职责，并努力传达出你具有灵活性。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Asking what your role will be suggests you will limit yourself purely to what is expected of you.","cn":"询问自己的职责是什么，会让人觉得你打算把自己严格限制在他人对你的期望之内。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"In reality, your role is whatever you make of it.","cn":"实际上，你的职责取决于你如何发挥。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"This is especially true in small companies, where the ability to adapt and take on new responsibilities is highly valued.","cn":"在小公司中尤其如此，因为适应变化并承担新的责任的能力备受重视。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"And this is equally important if you're just starting out.","cn":"如果你刚刚开始职业生涯，这一点同样重要。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Entry level interviewees would do well to demonstrate a broad set of skills in most interviews.","cn":"对于初级职位的面试者来说，在大多数面试中展示广泛的技能组合会很有帮助。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It's important to have a wide skill set as many startups and small companies are moving really fast.","cn":"拥有多方面的技能非常重要，因为许多初创公司和小公司发展得非常快。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Employers are looking for candidates that are intelligent and can quickly adapt and excel in a growing company.","cn":"雇主正在寻找聪明、能够迅速适应并在不断成长的公司中取得优异表现的候选人。"}]},{"id":"cet6-2021-12-2","level":"CET6","exam":"2021_12_2","year":2021,"month":12,"set":2,"type":"整卷听力","title":"2021年12月 六级第2套 · 听力真题","source":"2021年12月 CET-6 第2套 · 听力（本地原音 + 逐句原文）","audio":"assets/audio/2021/cet6-2021-12-set2.mp3","intro":"听力原文按录音篇目逐句拆分，中文译文仅供参考；音频为本地真题原音，整卷原音无法定位单句，逐句请用下方播放器。","questions":[],"lines":[{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Good morning and welcome to People in the News. With me today is Meghan Brown, an environmental activist whose controversial new book Beyond Recycling is making headlines.","cn":"M: 早上好，欢迎收看《新闻人物》。今天和我一起做节目的是 Meghan Brown，一位环保活动人士。她那本颇具争议的新书《Beyond Recycling》正在成为新闻焦点。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: Hi, Brian.","cn":"W: 你好，Brian。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Thanks for having me today.","cn":"谢谢你今天邀请我来。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"I'm excited to explain to the audience what my book is really about.","cn":"我很高兴能向观众解释我的书到底讲的是什么。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Critics of your book assert that you're trying to force radical changes on the entire country.","cn":"M: 批评你这本书的人声称，你试图迫使整个国家发生激进的改变。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Some claim that you want to force everyone to eat a vegetarian diet and make private transport illegal.","cn":"有人说，你想强迫所有人都吃素，并让私人交通工具变得非法。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I'm aware of those claims, but they simply aren't true.","cn":"W: 我知道这些说法，但它们根本不是真的。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"People who haven't read the book are making assumptions about my arguments.","cn":"那些没读过这本书的人在擅自揣测我的观点。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"They know I'm a vegetarian, that I don't wear leather or fur, and that I always use public transportation.","cn":"他们知道我是素食主义者，不穿皮革或皮草，而且总是乘坐公共交通。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"So they're depicting me as a radical animal rights activist and environmentalist determined to force my beliefs on others.","cn":"所以，他们把我描述成一个激进的动物权利活动人士和环保主义者，认定我决心把自己的信仰强加给别人。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: But don't you want others to adopt your practices?","cn":"M: 但你难道不希望别人也采取你的生活方式吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"You've campaigned for animal rights and the environment for decades.","cn":"你为动物权利和环境问题奔走了几十年。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I'd love it if people choose to live as I do.","cn":"W: 如果人们选择像我这样生活，我当然会很高兴。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But my life choices are based on my personal convictions.","cn":"但我的生活选择是基于我个人的信念。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"They aren't my recommendations for others who don't share those convictions.","cn":"对于那些不认同这些信念的人来说，这并不是我的建议。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: Well, in this excerpt from your book, you argue that meat consumption and private transport are devastating the environment and that the best choices for the planet are vegetarian diets and public transport.","cn":"M: 那么，在你书中的这段节选里，你认为食用肉类和使用私人交通工具正在严重破坏环境，而对地球来说，最好的选择是素食和公共交通。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: I did write that.","cn":"W: 我的确写了这些。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"But those are examples of what I call best practices, not what I'm actually suggesting.","cn":"但那只是我所说的最佳做法的例子，并不是我实际提出的建议。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"In my guidelines for saving the environment, I suggest modest changes, like eating vegetarian meals two days a week.","cn":"在我关于保护环境的指导中，我建议进行一些适度的改变，比如每周吃两天素食。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"M: You also endorse high taxes on meat and other animal products and increased taxes on gasoline.","cn":"M: 你还支持对肉类和其他动物制品征收高额税，并提高汽油税。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Those taxes could force poor people to adopt your life choices.","cn":"这些税收可能会迫使穷人采用你的生活方式。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"W: But the taxes I suggest aren't that high, less than 3% only.","cn":"W: 但我建议的税率并不高，只有不到3%。"},{"sp":"长对话 1","en":"Plus, the money generated would be allocated to environmental protection, which benefits everyone.","cn":"此外，筹集到的钱将用于环境保护，而这会让每个人都受益。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: With me in the studio today is Ms. Jane Logan, author of a new book, Secrets to Success.","cn":"M: 今天和我一起在演播室的是简·洛根女士，她是新书《成功的秘诀》的作者。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"She claims to have uncovered how people achieve success.","cn":"她声称自己已经揭示了人们取得成功的方式。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So Ms. Logan, in your book, you claim that successful people have many things in common.","cn":"那么，洛根女士，在您的书中，您声称成功人士有许多共同之处。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"For instance, they know their strengths when pursuing a goal.","cn":"比如说，他们在追求目标时清楚自己的优势。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: That's right.","cn":"W: 没错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"They also tend to be motivated by a negative or positive life event.","cn":"他们往往还会受到人生中某个积极或消极事件的激励。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"They credit their success to having someone in their life who believes in them.","cn":"他们把自己的成功归功于生命中有一个相信他们的人。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: You also write that there are a number of different factors related to success.","cn":"M: 您还写道，成功与许多不同因素有关。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And while successful people are driven to achieve their goals, the ultra successful have even greater ambition.","cn":"成功人士会努力实现自己的目标，而那些极其成功的人则有更大的抱负。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Yes, greater ambition as well as a burning desire to be the best of the best is also a common characteristic.","cn":"W: 是的，更大的抱负，以及成为最优秀中的最优秀者的强烈愿望，也是一个共同特征。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Right.","cn":"M: 没错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"So those who are determined don't see obstacles as something that prevents success, but mere inconveniences that need to be overcome.","cn":"所以，那些意志坚定的人不会把障碍看成阻止成功的东西，而只会把它们视为需要克服的不便。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Absolutely.","cn":"W: 当然。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Successful people are also optimistic as it is important to stay positive while being aware of obstacles that can deter us from achieving our goals.","cn":"成功人士也很乐观，因为在意识到可能阻碍我们实现目标的障碍的同时，保持积极的心态非常重要。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: That's a good point.","cn":"M: 说得好。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"All too often, people give up at the first hurdle.","cn":"人们往往在遇到第一个障碍时就放弃了。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Would you say then that most successful people make it all by themselves?","cn":"那么，您是否认为大多数成功人士都是完全靠自己取得成功的呢？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Not exactly.","cn":"W: 不完全是。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"They are usually good at cooperating with people and understanding the needs of others.","cn":"他们通常很善于与人合作，也善于理解他人的需求。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: So people will be willing to help them, I guess.","cn":"M: 所以我想，人们会愿意帮助他们。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: That's correct.","cn":"W: 没错。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"And this often leads to a great deal of mutual respect, whether it's with a colleague, an assistant or even a receptionist.","cn":"而且，这往往会带来极大的相互尊重，无论对方是同事、助理，还是前台接待员。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"M: Most successful people I know are very passionate about their work.","cn":"M: 我认识的大多数成功人士都对自己的工作充满热情。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"Would you say that passion is the single biggest key to success?","cn":"您认为热情是成功的最大关键吗？"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"W: Not entirely.","cn":"W: 不完全是。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"There's a prerequisite, that is, you have to work in an environment that nurtures passion.","cn":"有一个前提条件，也就是说，你必须在一个能够培养热情的环境中工作。"},{"sp":"长对话 2","en":"If that exists, success will follow.","cn":"如果这一点具备了，成功就会随之而来。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The saying \"blind as a bat\" simply isn't correct.","cn":"“像蝙蝠一样瞎”这种俗语根本不正确。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The truth is that all 1100 bat species can see and often their vision is pretty good, although not as excellent as other night-hunting animals.","cn":"事实是，所有1100种蝙蝠都有视力，而且它们的视力通常相当不错，尽管不如其他夜间捕猎的动物那样出色。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"There are two main groups of bats, which are believed to have evolved independently of each other, but both from a common ancestor.","cn":"蝙蝠主要分为两大类，据信它们是从共同祖先独立演化而来的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The first group, known as the mega bats, are mostly medium-sized or large bats who eat fruits, flowers, and sometimes small animals or fish.","cn":"第一类被称为大蝙蝠，大多是中型或大型蝙蝠，以水果、花朵为食，有时也吃小动物或鱼类。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"These species have distinctive visual centers and big eyes.","cn":"这些物种拥有独特的视觉中心和大眼睛。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"They use senses of vision and smell to capture their prey.","cn":"它们利用视觉和嗅觉来捕获猎物。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"For example, Flying Foxes not only see well during daylight, but can also distinguish colors.","cn":"例如，狐蝠不仅在白天视力良好，还能分辨颜色。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"They actually rely on their daylight vision and cannot fly during the night with no moonlight.","cn":"它们实际上依赖白天的视力，在没有月光的夜晚无法飞行。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"The second group, called micro bats, are smaller in size and mostly eat insects.","cn":"第二类被称为小蝙蝠，体型较小，主要以昆虫为食。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"These species use echolocation to find their way and identify food.","cn":"这些物种利用回声定位来辨别方向和识别食物。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Scientists have proven that despite their poorly developed small eyes, these bats still can see during the day.","cn":"科学家已经证实，尽管这些蝙蝠的小眼睛发育较差，但它们在白天仍然可以看到。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"When we consider the nightly lifestyle of these bats, we will see they have to be sensitive to the changing light levels because this is how they sense when to start hunting.","cn":"当我们考虑到这些蝙蝠的夜间生活方式时，就会发现它们必须对光线强度的变化保持敏感，因为它们正是以此感知何时开始捕猎。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Moreover, vision is used by micro bats to travel over long distances, beyond the range of echolocation.","cn":"此外，小蝙蝠还利用视觉进行长距离飞行，超出了回声定位的范围。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"So the truth is, there are no bats which are naturally blind.","cn":"因此事实是，没有天生失明的蝙蝠。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 1","en":"Some species use their sense of hearing more than their eyes as a matter of adaptation to a particular lifestyle, but their eyes are still functional.","cn":"出于对特定生活方式的适应，某些物种使用听觉多于眼睛，但它们的眼睛仍然具有功能。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"A study has found that educational TV shows come with an added lesson that influences the child's behavior.","cn":"一项研究发现，教育类电视节目还附带着一堂会影响儿童行为的课程。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Children who spend more time watching educational programs increase their emotional aggression toward other children.","cn":"花更多时间观看教育类节目的儿童，会增加对其他儿童的情绪性攻击行为。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"This shows that children can learn the educational lesson that was intended.","cn":"这表明，儿童能够学会节目原本 intended 的教育内容。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"However, they're also learning other things along the way.","cn":"然而，在此过程中，他们也会学到其他东西。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"This unintended impact has to do with the portrayal of conflict in media and how preschool-age children comprehend that conflict. TV and movie producers often incorporate an element of bad behavior. This is to teach children a lesson at the end of the program. Educational shows have pro-education and pro-social goals. However, conflict between characters is often depicted with characters being unkind to each other or they may use emotionally aggressive tactics with each other. Preschool children really don't get the moral of the story. That's because it requires that they understand how all the parts of the show fit together. You need pretty complicated cognitive skills and memory skills to be able to do that. These are still developing in young children.","cn":"这种非预期影响与媒体对冲突的呈现方式以及学龄前儿童对冲突的理解方式有关。电视和电影制作者经常加入不良行为元素，以便在节目结尾教给儿童一个道理。教育类节目具有促进教育和促进社会性发展的目标。然而，人物之间的冲突通常被刻画为人物彼此不友善，或者彼此采用情绪性攻击手段。学龄前儿童确实无法理解故事的寓意。这是因为他们需要理解节目中的各个部分是如何相互联系、共同构成整体的。要做到这一点，需要相当复杂的认知能力和记忆能力，而这些能力在幼儿身上仍在发展之中。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"However, parents shouldn't completely constrain children's viewing.","cn":"然而，家长不应该完全限制儿童观看电视。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Parents should instead watch with their kids and help them to understand the plot.","cn":"相反，家长应该陪孩子一起观看，并帮助他们理解情节。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"Parents can comment along the way and then explain the message at the end.","cn":"家长可以在观看过程中发表评论，然后在结尾解释其中传达的信息。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"They should explain how certain types of behavior were not appropriate.","cn":"他们应该说明某些行为方式为什么是不恰当的。"},{"sp":"听力篇章 2","en":"This will help children interpret and get the message and help them learn to watch the show for those messages.","cn":"这将帮助儿童理解并领会节目传达的信息，也帮助他们学会关注节目中的这些信息。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"While it has long been a practice in Asian countries, many people in Western countries have yet to embrace the no-shoes-in-the-house rule.","cn":"虽然在亚洲国家，无鞋入室长期以来一直是一种习惯，但许多西方国家的人仍未接受在屋内不穿鞋的规定。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"For many in those countries, wiping their shoes before going inside is regarded as sufficient.","cn":"对这些国家的许多人来说，进屋前擦擦鞋就被认为足够了。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"After all, they may think a little dirt doesn't hurt anyone.","cn":"毕竟，他们可能认为一点灰尘不会伤害任何人。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"But I can give you several good reasons why people should remove their shoes before going inside their homes.","cn":"但我可以给你几个人们进屋前应该脱鞋的充分理由。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Bacteria are everywhere.","cn":"细菌无处不在。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"They collect on your shoes when you walk along sidewalks, public toilet floors and even office carpets.","cn":"当你沿着人行道、公共厕所的地面，甚至办公室的地毯行走时，细菌会附着在你的鞋上。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"In one study conducted at an American university, researchers collected microscopic germs from footwear.","cn":"在一所美国大学开展的一项研究中，研究人员从鞋子上采集了微小的细菌。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"They found that up to 421,000 units of bacteria can collect on the outside of a single shoe.","cn":"他们发现，单只鞋子的外部最多可以聚集421,000个细菌单位。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"And it only takes a little bit of dirt to damage your timber floors.","cn":"而损坏木地板只需要一点点灰尘。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The more dirt you track in, the more it scratches and the more often you'd have to clean.","cn":"你带进屋里的灰尘越多，地板受到的刮擦就越严重，你需要清洁地板的频率也就越高。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The extra scrubbing will harm your floors over time.","cn":"额外的擦洗会随着时间的推移损坏地板。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Shoes can also leave marks and scratches on floors, especially high heels or shoes with pointed or hard parts.","cn":"鞋子也可能在地板上留下痕迹和划痕，尤其是高跟鞋或带有尖锐、坚硬部件的鞋子。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"These can dent and scratch your floor.","cn":"这些鞋子会使地板凹陷并留下划痕。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"And if you live in an apartment building, removing your noisy shoes is the polite thing to do out of consideration for your downstairs neighbors.","cn":"而且，如果你住在公寓楼里，考虑到楼下邻居，脱掉发出声响的鞋子是一种礼貌的做法。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Walking around with bare feet is actually better for your feet.","cn":"实际上，赤脚走路对你的双脚更有益。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"It strengthens the muscles in your feet.","cn":"它能增强脚部肌肉。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Though many people are accustomed to wearing shoes during all their waking hours, the more time you spend wearing shoes, the more likely you are to incur foot injuries as a result.","cn":"尽管许多人已经习惯在清醒的所有时间里都穿鞋，但你穿鞋的时间越长，就越有可能因此受到足部伤害。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"And if people aren't yet convinced by my arguments, I can give one final reason.","cn":"如果人们还没有被我的论据说服，我还可以给出最后一个理由。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"The dust and toxic chemicals you bring into your house via your shoes can deteriorate the air quality in your home.","cn":"你通过鞋子带进屋里的灰尘和有毒化学物质会降低家中的空气质量。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Toxic chemicals are everywhere in our lives: insect-killing chemicals used on public grass areas, cleaning chemicals on the floors of public areas.","cn":"有毒化学物质遍布我们的生活：公共草地上使用的杀虫剂，公共场所地面上的清洁剂。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"By kicking off your shoes before you enter the home, you are denying entry to these harmful chemicals.","cn":"进屋前脱掉鞋子，就能阻止这些有害化学物质进入室内。"},{"sp":"讲座 1","en":"Given the amount of time we spend in classrooms, and the number of shoes that pass through them every day, you may well understand me if I were to propose a no-shoes-in-the-classroom rule.","cn":"考虑到我们在教室里度过的时间，以及每天经过教室的鞋子数量，如果我提议制定教室内不穿鞋的规定，你很可能会理解我。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Emotions are an essential and inseparable part of our consciousness.","cn":"情绪是我们意识中不可或缺且无法分割的一部分。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"They are part of a built-in mechanism, which allows us to cope with the ups and downs of our lives both physically and mentally.","cn":"它们是与生俱来的机制的一部分，使我们能够在身心两方面应对生活中的起起落落。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"When we hide our emotions and our true feelings, we stop being genuine, spontaneous and authentic in our relationships.","cn":"当我们隐藏自己的情绪和真实感受时，我们在与他人的关系中便不再真诚、自然和真实。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"When we put on cultivated and polished faces in the company of others, we stop being true to ourselves.","cn":"当我们在他人面前摆出经过刻意修饰和精心打磨的面孔时，我们便不再忠于自我。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Socially, it may be a good tactic to hide our true emotions, but morally it is also a breach of faith and trust.","cn":"从社会角度看，隐藏真实情绪可能是一种有效的策略，但从道德角度看，这也违背了信任和诚信。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Although humans are more advanced and intelligent, animals are more genuine and authentic in their behavior and responses than human beings.","cn":"尽管人类更加先进、更加聪明，但动物在行为和反应上比人类更加真诚、更加真实。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"The more educated we are, the less transparent and reliable we become.","cn":"我们受教育程度越高，就越不透明，也越不可靠。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"We are drawn to our pets because pets do not lie.","cn":"我们会被自己的宠物吸引，是因为宠物不会撒谎。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"One of the first steps in dealing with emotions such as anger or fear is to acknowledge them as normal and human.","cn":"处理愤怒或恐惧等情绪的第一步之一，是承认它们是正常的人类情感。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"There is nothing sinful or immoral about being emotional, unless your emotions make you inhuman, insensitive and cruel to others.","cn":"情绪化本身没有任何罪恶或不道德之处，除非你的情绪使你变得不人道、麻木不仁并且残酷地对待他人。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Feelings of guilt associated with emotions are more devastating and damaging than the experience of emotion itself.","cn":"与情绪相关的内疚感，比情绪本身的体验更具破坏性，也更令人痛苦。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"So when you deal with the problem of emotions, you should learn not only how to control them but also how to accept them and manage the guilt and anguish arising from them.","cn":"因此，当你处理情绪问题时，不仅要学会如何控制情绪，还要学会如何接受情绪，并管理由此产生的内疚和苦恼。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Our brains are made up of a primitive inner core and a more evolved and rational outer core.","cn":"我们的大脑由一个原始的内部核心和一个进化程度更高、更具理性的外部核心组成。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Most of the time, the rational part of the mind controls the information coming from the primitive core and makes its own decisions as to what to do and how to respond.","cn":"大多数时候，心智中理性的部分会控制来自原始核心的信息，并自行决定该做什么以及如何回应。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"However, during critical situations, especially when a threat is perceived, the outer core loses control and fails to regulate the impulses and instinctual responses coming from the primitive brain.","cn":"然而，在关键情境下，尤其是在察觉到威胁时，外部核心会失去控制，无法调节来自原始大脑的冲动和本能反应。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"As a result, we let disturbing thoughts and emotions arise in our consciousness and surrender to our primitive behavior.","cn":"结果，我们让令人不安的思想和情绪进入意识，并屈从于原始的行为方式。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"In times of emotional turmoil, remember that emotions arise because your senses are wired to the primitive part of your mind which is self-regulated, autonomous and spontaneous.","cn":"在情绪动荡时期，请记住，情绪之所以产生，是因为你的感官与心智中那个具有自我调节能力、自主性和自发性的原始部分相连。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"Your rational mind does not always deal with the messages coming from it effectively.","cn":"你的理性思维并不总能有效处理来自这一部分的信息。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"These messages are part of your survival mechanism and should not be stifled simply because emotions are unhealthy and betray your weaknesses.","cn":"这些信息是你生存机制的一部分，不应仅仅因为情绪不健康、会暴露你的弱点，就被压抑。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"When emotions arise, instead of stifling them, pay attention to them and try to understand the messages they are trying to deliver.","cn":"当情绪出现时，不要压抑它们，而要关注它们，并努力理解它们试图传达的信息。"},{"sp":"讲座 2","en":"This way you make use of your emotions without losing your balance and inner stability.","cn":"这样，你就能利用自己的情绪，同时不失去平衡和内在的稳定。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Good morning, class.","cn":"同学们，早上好。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"My topic today is how to feed a hungry world.","cn":"今天我要讲的主题是如何养活一个饥饿的世界。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The world's population is expected to grow from 6.8 billion today to 9.1 billion by 2050.","cn":"预计世界人口将从目前的68亿增长到2050年的91亿。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Meanwhile, the world's population more than doubled from 3 billion between 1961 and 2007.","cn":"与此同时，世界人口在1961年至2007年间从30亿增加了一倍多。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Simultaneously, food production has been constrained by a lack of scientific research.","cn":"与此同时，粮食生产又受到科学研究不足的限制。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Still, the task of feeding the world's population in 2050 seems easily possible.","cn":"尽管如此，到2050年养活世界人口似乎仍然完全可行。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"What is needed is a second green revolution.","cn":"我们需要的是第二次绿色革命。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"This is an approach that is described as the sustainable growth of global agriculture.","cn":"这是一种被称为全球农业可持续增长的方式。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Such a revolution will require a wholesale shift of priorities in agricultural research.","cn":"这样的革命需要彻底改变农业研究的优先事项。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"There is an urgent need for new crop varieties.","cn":"人们迫切需要培育新的作物品种。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"They must offer higher yields but use less water, nitrogen-rich fertilizers or other inputs.","cn":"这些品种必须提高产量，同时减少对水、富含氮的肥料或其他投入品的使用。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"These new crops must also be more resistant to drought, heat and pests.","cn":"这些新品种还必须更能抵抗干旱、高温和害虫。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Equally crucial is lower-tech research into basics such as crop rotation and mixed farming of animals and plants on small farms.","cn":"同样重要的是开展技术含量较低的研究，探讨作物轮作以及小农场中动植物混合养殖等基础问题。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Developing nations could score substantial gains in productivity by making better use of modern technologies and practices.","cn":"发展中国家可以通过更好地利用现代技术和生产实践，大幅提高生产率。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But that requires money.","cn":"但这需要资金。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It is estimated that to meet the 2050 challenge, investment must double to 83 billion US dollars a year.","cn":"据估计，为应对2050年的挑战，投资必须翻一番，达到每年830亿美元。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Most of that money needs to go towards improving agricultural infrastructure.","cn":"其中大部分资金需要用于改善农业基础设施。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Everything from production to storage and processing must improve.","cn":"从生产到储存和加工的各个环节都必须得到改进。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"However, research agendas need to be focused on the needs of the poorest and most resource-limited countries.","cn":"然而，研究议程需要着眼于最贫困且资源最有限国家的需求。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"It is there that most of the world's population lives and it is there the population growth over the next decades will be the greatest.","cn":"世界上大多数人口生活在那里，未来几十年人口增长最为迅速的地方也在那里。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"To their credit, the world's agricultural scientists are embracing such a broad view.","cn":"值得肯定的是，世界各国的农业科学家正在采取这样广泛的视角。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"In March, for example, they came together at the first Global Conference on Agricultural Research to begin working out how to change research agendas to help meet the needs of farmers in poorer nations.","cn":"例如，今年3月，他们齐聚首届全球农业研究大会，开始研究如何改变研究议程，以帮助满足较贫困国家农民的需求。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But these plans will not bear fruit unless they get considerably more support from policy-makers.","cn":"但是，除非得到政策制定者大力增加的支持，这些计划将不会结出成果。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The growth in public agricultural-research spending peaked in the 1970s and has been shrinking ever since.","cn":"公共农业研究支出的增长在20世纪70年代达到顶峰，此后一直在缩减。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"The big exception is China, where spending has far surpassed other countries over the past decade.","cn":"中国是一个明显的例外，过去十年中，中国的相关支出已经远远超过其他国家。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"China seems set to transition to become the key supplier of relevant science and technology to poorer countries.","cn":"中国似乎将转型为向较贫困国家提供相关科学技术的主要供应者。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"But developed countries have a humanitarian responsibility too.","cn":"但发达国家同样负有提供人道主义援助的责任。"},{"sp":"讲座 3","en":"Calls by scientists for large increases in the appropriation of funds for public spending on agricultural research are more than justified.","cn":"科学家们呼吁大幅增加公共农业研究支出的拨款，这一要求完全合理。"}]}];
